/* 5-letter-cap stories: 300 parodies, generated by tools/build-word-readers.mjs from library/word-stories.json. Do not edit. */
window.READERS.push(
  { id: "w5-043-the-hero-with-a-receipt", title: "The hero with a receipt", pay: 15390, lib: 5, text: "Pip saves a crown from a well. He hands it to May with a wet paw. His tail drips, and his fur reeks of moss. May gives him any prize he wants. The troop waits for him to ask for gold. Pip asks for a fence round the well. May nods. Next week he saves her fence from the same well." },
  { id: "w5-042-the-royal-bath-lake", title: "The royal bath lake", pay: 15390, lib: 5, text: "Rex wants a bath as wide as a lake. The troop digs one, and rain fills it. Rex dips a paw in. He jumps back. He puts his tail in and pulls it right out. The lake is far too cold. Dot hands him a pot. Rex heats one cup of lake water and takes a royal bath in his old bowl." },
  { id: "w5-037-the-castle-with-round-discs", title: "The castle with round discs", pay: 15390, lib: 5, text: "Ned makes a fort on discs. The troop rolls it up a hill to gain a grand view. Ned has dust in his fur and a sore paw. His tail slips off the brake. The fort rolls down to the lake. It bobs. Ned calls it a royal barge. Dot asks for a ride, then notes that the seat is now the drain." },
  { id: "w5-052-the-whistle-in-the-cake", title: "The whistle in the cake", pay: 15390, lib: 5, text: "Dot hears a high note at the bake sale. Each time Ned takes a bite, it sings again. She asks him to open his mouth. There is a small pipe in his cake. The troop knows whose it is. Rex has lost his pipe for the race. He must now ask Ned to chew when it is time to start." },
  { id: "w5-103-the-star-that-blinked", title: "The star that blinked", pay: 15390, lib: 5, text: "May saw a star blink three times. She sent her troop to help. Their ship flew close and found Ned in a tin shed. He had run out of light bulbs. He waved a torch to ask for a spare. May gave him a bulb and asked about the star. Ned held up a glass. He had hoped to read by the stars." },
  { id: "w5-026-the-map-that-folds", title: "The map that folds", pay: 15660, lib: 5, text: "Pip has a map of the whole realm. He folds it to fit his paw. Now the sea lies next to the seat. The troop takes a boat to the king. Pip has salt in his fur and a wet tail. The king asks how they got past his walls. Pip opens the map. They all land in the royal bath." },
  { id: "w5-028-the-quiet-horn", title: "The quiet horn", pay: 15660, lib: 5, text: "Ned buys a horn to call his troop on a quest. He blows so hard his teeth ache. No sound comes out. Dot puts a paw in the horn and finds a sock. Ned pulls it out with his tail. Now the horn works. The troop comes up to the hill. The quest is to find the owner of a very ripe sock." },
  { id: "w5-123-the-frog-exam", title: "The frog exam", pay: 15660, lib: 5, text: "May had to turn a cup into a frog. She cast her spell and heard a croak. The troop gave a cheer. Ivy asked her to lift the cup. A real frog sat below it. May had found it in the pond. Ivy said the test was not done. May made the frog a cup at last, then gave tea to a very dazed class." },
  { id: "w5-029-the-tiny-curse", title: "The tiny curse", pay: 15660, lib: 5, text: "Ivy puts a spell on Rex to make him small. He hides in her fur and nips her tail. The troop can hear his laugh but can not see him. Ivy asks him to stop. Rex asks for a crumb in each paw. She gives him a whole cake. He says the spell must stay till he can eat it all." },
  { id: "w5-005-the-frog-on-strike", title: "The frog on strike", pay: 15660, lib: 5, text: "A frog asked Ivy for a kiss. Ivy said she could give him a plum. He took it and asked for more. Soon the troop sat by the pool with fruit in each paw. Ivy wiped juice from her fur and hid her tail. The frog would not turn into a lord. He liked free lunch far more than he liked a crown." },
  { id: "w5-101-the-moon-rent", title: "The moon rent", pay: 15660, lib: 5, text: "Pip put his flag on the moon. His troop had a fine new home. Then Dot came out of a cave with a bill. She had got there first and owned the land. Pip had no gold, so he gave her his flag. Dot used it as a mop. The moon was dusty, and rent was now one clean cave each month." },
  { id: "w5-004-the-bean-fare", title: "The bean fare", pay: 15660, lib: 5, text: "Gus sold a cow for a sack of beans. The beans grew a stalk up to a cloud. Gus went up with his tail round each leaf and dew in his fur. A huge paw held out a fare chart. The cloud troop ran a lift now. Gus had no coins, so he gave the lift a scrub and rode down with a mop as his prize." },
  { id: "w5-058-the-extra-tennis-ball", title: "The extra tennis ball", pay: 15660, lib: 5, text: "Rex wins each point with a fresh ball. The troop sees a sly trick. Dot peers into his pouch. It is empty. Rex puts up both paws with a grin. Gus looks at his tail. It holds a tube of balls out of sight. Rex gets a new job. He now feeds balls to the whole troop and wins no games at all." },
  { id: "w5-001-the-crown-that-rang", title: "The crown that rang", pay: 15660, lib: 5, text: "Pip found a gold crown in a tree. Each time he put it on, it rang like a bell. The troop came to bow, then held their ears. Pip hid his tail in his fur and tried to look grand. Dot gave the crown a tap with her paw. A bee flew out. Its hive had a new king, and that king owed rent." },
  { id: "w5-050-the-royal-image-itch", title: "The royal image itch", pay: 15660, lib: 5, text: "Rex sits for a grand image. He keeps his tail rigid and his paw on a gold ball. His skin grows itchy. He moves. The troop tells him to hold still. Dot draws each pose on a fresh sheet. Rex sees a blur of arms when she flips them. He buys the whole stack and calls it his first royal film show." },
  { id: "w5-108-the-robot-tail", title: "The robot tail", pay: 15930, lib: 5, text: "Gus made a robot to brush his fur. It did a fine job till it saw his tail. It saw the tail as a rope and tied it to the chair. The troop set Gus free. Dot used a doll to teach the robot about tails. Now it combs the doll all day. Gus sits next to it and waits for his turn." },
  { id: "w5-039-the-quest-of-the-spare-sock", title: "The quest of the spare sock", pay: 15930, lib: 5, text: "Bo seeks the mate to his sock. He asks each one of the troop to lift a paw. No luck. His tail drags in mud and his fur fills with burrs. At dusk he sits on a stump and sighs. The sock hangs on his own tail. He puts it on at last, then finds he has lost the other one." },
  { id: "w5-031-the-king-of-puddles", title: "The king of puddles", pay: 15930, lib: 5, text: "Rex calls a pool his realm. He puts a flag in it with his paw. The troop bows, but Dot grins into her fur. Rex curls his tail on his new seat. Then the sun dries the pool. Rex moves his flag to a cup of tea. Dot sips it. His next realm has a lid and a sign that says do not sip." },
  { id: "w5-132-the-comet-hairbrush", title: "The comet hairbrush", pay: 16200, lib: 5, text: "Ivy took a brush from a comet. The brush made her fur glow. Her troop could see her all night. She liked it till she tried to hide in a game. Dot found her in the dark shed at once. Ivy gave the brush to the lamps in the hall. Now the lamps glow, and Ivy can hide till her tail pokes out." },
  { id: "w5-083-the-cricket-tea-break", title: "The cricket tea break", pay: 16200, lib: 5, text: "Rex bats a ball into the tea pot. The troop calls it out. Rex says the pot is still on the field. Dot pours the tea and the ball rolls into a cup. Gus sips his tea and spits the ball back onto the pitch. The judge halts the game to give a rule. The rest drink all the tea while he reads." },
  { id: "w5-040-the-oath-at-lunch", title: "The oath at lunch", pay: 16200, lib: 5, text: "Gus vows to guard a pie till the troop comes home. He sets his paw on his chest. His fur is neat and his tail is still. A fly lands on the crust. Gus eats that bit to save the pie. A new fly lands. By dusk only the dish is left. Gus waits proud by it. No fly has hurt the dish." },
  { id: "w5-104-the-space-suit-zipper", title: "The space suit zipper", pay: 16200, lib: 5, text: "Bo wore his new suit to step out of the ship. His tail stuck out of the back. The troop could not close the seal. Dot put a pipe over the tail and fixed a cap on it. Bo went out and waved. He used his new tail pipe to hook lost bolts. Dot made him chief of all ship tool work." },
  { id: "w5-124-the-flying-broom-closet", title: "The flying broom closet", pay: 16200, lib: 5, text: "Ned chose a broom from the class shed. He rode it to the sky. The troop saw the broom shake free. Ned clung to a cloud and held on. Ivy sent up a mop. Ned flew home on it and asked why the broom had fled. It still had its price tag. The shop asked for it back till he paid the bill." },
  { id: "w5-038-the-jewel-in-the-soup", title: "The jewel in the soup", pay: 16200, lib: 5, text: "Ivy finds a red gem in her soup. She holds it up with her paw. The troop roars. Her tail waves, and her fur glows in the light. Rex says the gem once sat in his crown. He takes it and puts it on his head. The gem pops. Red juice runs down his nose. Ivy asks for her plum back." },
  { id: "w5-036-the-north-wind-scarf", title: "The north wind scarf", pay: 16200, lib: 5, text: "The wind tries to pull a scarf off Bo. Bo grips it with one paw and holds his tail tight. His fur stays warm. The sun tries next. Bo opens the scarf but puts on a shade hat. The troop bets on who will win. Dot gives Bo a plum. He takes off the scarf to make a fruit bag. Dot keeps the bets." },
  { id: "w5-048-the-spell-in-the-jam", title: "The spell in the jam", pay: 16200, lib: 5, text: "Ivy makes jam that lets each eater sing. Gus tries it, and his voice fills the room. Each note makes his chest shake. His tail keeps time. The troop holds paws over their ears. Ivy puts the lid back on the jar. The jar sings too. Gus takes it on stage and lets it do all the hard high notes." },
  { id: "w5-045-the-gift-that-glows", title: "The gift that glows", pay: 16200, lib: 5, text: "Ned gets a stone that glows at night. He shows the troop and puts it under his bed. His fur glows blue, and his tail casts a long shade. He hides his eyes with a paw. He can not sleep. Dot buys the stone to light her shed. Ned gets a plain dark rock for his bed and has the best night in years." },
  { id: "w5-086-the-wrong-scent", title: "The wrong scent", pay: 16200, lib: 5, text: "Dot takes a trail of roast nuts. She hopes to find the lost snack box. The troop waits at the shed. Dot finds a bath, where Rex has nut soap in his fur. He shows her the box by the tub. He used its lid as a tray. Dot finds the nuts in the soap dish and asks Rex which ones he ate." },
  { id: "w5-095-the-case-of-the-red-moon", title: "The case of the red moon", pay: 16200, lib: 5, text: "May sees a red moon above the shed. She calls Dot to solve the odd sight. The troop comes in fear. Dot walks up to it with a stick. The moon hangs from a cord. It is a red globe Rex got for his play. May asks why it has teeth. Rex says the crowd got bored with his plain old moon last week." },
  { id: "w5-105-the-crater-cake", title: "The crater cake", pay: 16200, lib: 5, text: "Rex found a round hole on the moon. The troop dug down and found a cake tin. Rex said the moon must be one huge cake. Dot took a bite of a rock and spat it out. Pip came from the ship with flour on his fur. He had tried to bake a cake out there. It flew away, and only the tin came back." },
  { id: "w5-002-a-pea-with-a-plan", title: "A pea with a plan", pay: 16200, lib: 5, text: "Dot slept on a stack of beds to prove her rank. A pea lay at the base. She felt no lump, but her tail hung down and her paw hit the floor. At dawn the troop found green vines all in her fur. The pea had grown up the beds. Dot won the test, then made the royal chef mow her room." },
  { id: "w5-010-the-dragon-candle", title: "The dragon candle", pay: 16200, lib: 5, text: "Dot met a beast with smoke in its nose. The troop hid, but Dot held up a cake. She asked it to light the wick. It blew once. Her fur got warm and her tail rose. She gave a glad clap. The beast had hoped to guard gold. Soon it stood at the cake shop, with a line of cakes and a sign for tips." },
  { id: "w5-015-the-troll-toll-book", title: "The troll toll book", pay: 16200, lib: 5, text: "Bo asked for a toll at his span. Each guest had to tell a joke. Gus gave him one about a tail in a pie. Bo had a laugh and let the troop pass. Then he saw Gus come back with fake fur and a new hat. Gus told the same joke. Bo put a paw out for coins. His span now had a fee for old jokes." },
  { id: "w5-034-the-crown-of-ants", title: "The crown of ants", pay: 16200, lib: 5, text: "Pip wins a crown of leaf bits at the fair. The troop lifts him high. His tail curls with pride. Then his skin grows itchy. He feels ants on each paw. The crown was their old roof. Pip sets it on a stump. He makes a fresh crown from paper. The ants vote him king again, for his fine grasp of home care." },
  { id: "w5-035-the-false-last-page", title: "The false last page", pay: 16200, lib: 5, text: "May reads that her tale must end with a feast. She cooks for the troop and wipes her fur clean. Her tail holds the spoon as her paw turns the last page. There is one more page. It says wash up. May tears it out and makes a paper crown. At the feast, she names Gus king of all the dirty bowls." },
  { id: "w5-046-the-cloud-steps", title: "The cloud steps", pay: 16200, lib: 5, text: "May ties ropes to make tall steps up to a cloud. The troop holds the base. Her tail curls round each rung, and her fur fills with mist. She puts a paw out at the top. The cloud moves. May sways over the town. She lets go above a pool. The troop calls it a bad quest, but May sells seats for the ride." },
  { id: "w5-121-the-spell-for-toast", title: "The spell for toast", pay: 16200, lib: 5, text: "Ivy told the class to turn bread into toast. Pip waved his wand and said roast. His whole desk grew hot. The troop let air in the door to drive smoke out. Ivy gave him a plain pan. Pip made toast in it while the rest did magic. His was the only meal free of frogs, fire, or bits of desk." },
  { id: "w5-054-the-high-jump-crown", title: "The high jump crown", pay: 16470, lib: 5, text: "Bo tries to jump over a pole. His tail hooks it on each try. The troop says he must tuck his tail. Bo does, but now he lands flat. Dot puts the pole on the grass and asks him to lift it. He lifts it past his head. He wins the high lift prize. The jump judge asks where the pole went." },
  { id: "w5-106-the-alien-welcome-mat", title: "The alien welcome mat", pay: 16470, lib: 5, text: "Ivy put a mat by the ship door. It said wipe paws. A new guest had ten feet and no paws. The troop had to wait while he wiped each toe. Ivy took the mat away. The guest went in and left a trail of mud. Ivy wrote a new sign. It said take off boots. The guest left ten boots by the tea tray." },
  { id: "w5-059-the-case-of-the-loud-sock", title: "The case of the loud sock", pay: 16470, lib: 5, text: "A chirp keeps the troop awake. Dot looks at the gate, the beds, and the roof. Pip walks with her. Each time he moves, the chirp moves too. She lifts one of his feet and finds a toy duck in his sock. Pip says he put it there to keep it safe. Dot gives the duck a nest. It gives her one last chirp." },
  { id: "w5-100-the-baton-in-the-bread", title: "The baton in the bread", pay: 16470, lib: 5, text: "May gives the baton to Bo. He runs to the goal, but the judge says no. Bo holds a loaf. The troop mixed up the snack bag and the race bag. May runs back to fetch the baton. She finds Gus with jam on it. The judge waits while they wash it, then gives the troop a prize for a very slow clean pass." },
  { id: "w5-113-the-polite-boarding-party", title: "The polite boarding party", pay: 16470, lib: 5, text: "May put her paw on a ship rail and asked to come on board. Its troop said yes. She asked for the gold. They said no. May gave a bow and went back to her boat. Gus asked where the loot was. May held up a cake. The ship had given her tea, and she had found the gold was just a cheap foil trim." },
  { id: "w5-049-the-brave-broom", title: "The brave broom", pay: 16470, lib: 5, text: "Dot asks a broom to sweep the hall. It tries to clean her tail as well. She holds a paw in front of her face and sends the broom out the door. The troop sees it clean the path, the hill, and the whole town. Dot gives it a tiny brush. At last it sits down to clean the dust from its own straw." },
  { id: "w5-008-the-cloak-with-pockets", title: "The cloak with pockets", pay: 16470, lib: 5, text: "Rex got a cloak no one could see. He wore it to meet the troop. His fur was cold, and his tail shook. Ned gave him a real coat. Rex put his paw into its deep pouch and found a note from the cloak shop. It said the cloak was free, but the pouch cost gold. Ned used the note to light the stove." },
  { id: "w5-089-the-bowling-alley-hill", title: "The bowling alley hill", pay: 16470, lib: 5, text: "May rolls a ball down the lane. It turns left and hits the shoe rack. The troop tries again with a new ball. The same thing takes place. Dot puts one paw on the floor. The lane tilts to the door. Gus set one leg of it on a plum. They take out the plum. May bowls a great game while Gus eats the plum." },
  { id: "w5-128-the-gravity-switch", title: "The gravity switch", pay: 16470, lib: 5, text: "Ned found a red lever on the ship. He hit it to make tea. The troop rose from their seats and hit the roof. Ned hung by his tail and tried to reach the lever again. Dot threw a shoe at it. They fell back down. The tea was still cold, so Ned wrote do not use for tea on the red lever." },
  { id: "w5-007-the-crumb-map", title: "The crumb map", pay: 16470, lib: 5, text: "Pip left bits to mark his trail. Dot ate them as they went. By dusk their troop was lost. Pip waved his tail and shook his fur. Dot put a paw on a tree. It had jam on its bark. She had wiped her paws on each tree after each snack. They went home by the jam trail and had soup for tea." },
  { id: "w5-071-the-secret-pie-code", title: "The secret pie code", pay: 16470, lib: 5, text: "Gus gets a note that says pie twice. Dot calls it a code. The troop tries each mark on the shed lock. No code works. Dot folds the note and finds jam on its pages. Gus has sent his own wish list. He lost the first note, so he wrote a new one. Dot opens the shed with the key taped to the list." },
  { id: "w5-084-the-clue-with-teeth", title: "The clue with teeth", pay: 16470, lib: 5, text: "May finds bite marks on the gate. Dot asks the troop to show their teeth. Each grin is too small. Gus shows them a saw. The marks match its teeth. May had asked him to make the gate lower, then lost track. Dot says the case is done. Gus asks if she means the gate. He has cut its latch in half." },
  { id: "w5-102-the-floating-soup", title: "The floating soup", pay: 16470, lib: 5, text: "Gus made soup on the ship. He took off the lid, and a warm blob rose into the air. The troop tried to catch it in bowls. Gus held a spoon in each paw but got no soup. Dot set a fan to blow. The soup blew into the air vent. Gus set cups below it. Lunch came from the roof with a fine gust." },
  { id: "w5-153-the-chair-promotion", title: "The chair promotion", pay: 16470, lib: 5, text: "Pip got a new rank at work. His desk was small, but his chair grew tall. The troop had to look up to speak to him. Pip could not reach his files. Dot put steps by his chair. He went down each time a task came in. By dusk he gave the chair his rank and sat on a stool to do the work." },
  { id: "w5-027-the-royal-soup-trial", title: "The royal soup trial", pay: 16470, lib: 5, text: "May sets a test for each brave beau. Each must eat her soup. Gus dips one paw in the bowl and loses some fur. His tail goes stiff. The troop begs him to stop. He asks May for bread to cool the soup. She gets a loaf. He finds her lost ring in it and wins her nod, plus lunch for the troop." },
  { id: "w5-003-the-shoe-fits-the-tree", title: "The shoe fits the tree", pay: 16470, lib: 5, text: "May left a glass shoe at the ball. Rex took it round the troop to find its mate. Each paw was too wide. Each tail got in the way. May saw him try the shoe on a limb and had to laugh till her fur shook. It fit the tree just right. Rex gave the tree a dance, while May went home in boots." },
  { id: "w5-018-the-ginger-loaf-ferry", title: "The ginger loaf ferry", pay: 16470, lib: 5, text: "A loaf ran from the oven and dared the troop to catch it. Pip used his tail to swing ahead. Dot held out one paw, but the loaf got past her. It came to a pond and asked Gus for a ride. Gus had flour in his fur and a boat full of buns. The loaf took one look, went home, and chose a cool shelf." },
  { id: "w5-110-the-silent-comet", title: "The silent comet", pay: 16470, lib: 5, text: "Pip led the troop to hear a comet sing. They wore ear cups and sat in space for hours. No song came. Dot asked Pip who said a comet sings. He gave her a book of poems. She gave him a drum and asked him to make the score. The comet went past to a fine beat. Pip sold the drum track with his quiet film." },
  { id: "w5-012-the-wish-coin-back", title: "The wish coin back", pay: 16740, lib: 5, text: "Ivy paid for a lamp and made a wish for gold. A gold fish came out. She made a wish for a crown. A crown of weeds fell on her fur. Her tail shook. The troop said to try once more. Ivy put her paw on the lamp and made a wish for a coin back. A coin fell out. She got a plain lamp that did what lamps ought to do." },
  { id: "w5-025-the-cloak-of-good-manners", title: "The cloak of good manners", pay: 16740, lib: 5, text: "Dot wore a cloak that said \"May I\" each time she moved. The troop liked it at first. Then her tail hit a door. \"May I?\" She gave her fur a rub. \"May I?\" She held a paw to eat. \"May I?\" Dot gave the cloak to a shop bell. It said \"May I\" when pals came in. At night she shut the shop and heard it say \"May I\" to each moth." },
  { id: "w5-033-the-wish-for-silence", title: "The wish for silence", pay: 16740, lib: 5, text: "Dot asks a star for quiet. The troop falls mute. Her tail makes no swish, and her paw makes no tap. Even her fur can not swish. Dot likes it till the tea boils. She can not hear the pot. She waves for her next wish. Sound comes back just as the pot tips. The star gives her a mop as a free third wish." },
  { id: "w5-152-the-cake-procurement-trial", title: "The cake procurement trial", pay: 16740, lib: 5, text: "May asked for cake for the staff feast. Ned said she had to get three bids. She asked the troop for bids. Gus said cake is nice. Dot said cake is round. Bo said cake is gone. Ned put each bid in a file and gave his stamp. May held out the empty tin. Bo had given the most exact quote of all." },
  { id: "w5-125-the-potion-label", title: "The potion label", pay: 16740, lib: 5, text: "Gus made a green drink for his class. Ivy said it would make fur glow. The troop took a sip and got shiny lips. Gus read his label. It said lips, not fur. Ivy made him write each label twice next time. Gus made plain water and gave it two tags. The class read both and still asked which spell would make them shine." },
  { id: "w5-051-the-missing-goal", title: "The missing goal", pay: 16740, lib: 5, text: "The troop comes to play ball, but the goal is gone. Pip finds two long marks in the mud. The marks lead to a shed. Gus sits there with the goal round his bed. He says it keeps flies off. Pip finds the net full of fruit. Gus is glad to move his bed to the field. Now each goal earns a free plum." },
  { id: "w5-146-the-pirate-eye-patch-swap", title: "The pirate eye patch swap", pay: 16740, lib: 5, text: "Ned put on an eye patch to look bold. He hit a mast. The troop gave him a cane, but he hit a rail next. Dot found that Ned had put the patch over his good eye. He moved it to the other side and saw the whole deck. Now he could steer the ship, while Dot used the cane to hang his wet socks." },
  { id: "w5-011-the-sword-in-the-loaf", title: "The sword in the loaf", pay: 16740, lib: 5, text: "Ned drew a blade from a loaf. The troop named him as king. He wiped flour from his fur with one paw and held his tail high. The baker came out and asked for his knife. Ned gave it back. The troop still bowed. The baker made him king of the wash bowl, where he ruled ten bowls and a spoon with jam on it." },
  { id: "w5-016-the-seven-small-seats", title: "The seven small seats", pay: 16740, lib: 5, text: "May found a hut with seven seats. She sat on one and broke it. Her tail sent two more down. A nail tore her coat. The troop came home to find her on the floor. May held a bent peg in her paw. She fixed each chair, then made one big bench. The troop sat on it and asked her to break the table too." },
  { id: "w5-080-the-case-of-the-wet-stamp", title: "The case of the wet stamp", pay: 16740, lib: 5, text: "Gus says a thief took his note. Dot looks in the post bag. It is full of wet paper. The troop used the bag as a rain hood. Gus holds up his paw and says his note was dry. Dot reads his name on the hood. The ink has run, but his words are clear. He asked the troop to bring him a dry coat." },
  { id: "w5-172-the-safe-with-a-window", title: "The safe with a window", pay: 16740, lib: 5, text: "Rex built a safe no thief could crack. He made a pane so the troop could view the gold. Dot asked if the glass was tough. Rex said no one had tried it yet. Bo hit it with a spoon. The gold fell out. Rex added a cloth and said the flaw was fixed. Dot put the spoon back and took her gold to a new bank." },
  { id: "w5-112-the-map-on-the-sail", title: "The map on the sail", pay: 16740, lib: 5, text: "Rex drew a map on his sail so he could not lose it. The troop set off to find the gold. Wind blew in the sail, and the map went round a pole. Rex could see only half. Dot cut a small map from paper. Rex said that might blow away. Dot put it in a box. Rex did not know maps could fit in boxes." },
  { id: "w5-154-the-zero-inbox-contest", title: "The zero inbox contest", pay: 16740, lib: 5, text: "Rex gave a prize for an empty inbox. The troop raced to clear their mail. Gus put his box in a bin. Dot sent all hers to Rex. May made a new box with no lid, so notes fell out. Rex won the prize, since his desk broke under all the notes. His box now lay flat under the floor, where no mail could fit." },
  { id: "w5-013-the-red-hood-feast", title: "The red hood feast", pay: 16740, lib: 5, text: "Dot wore a red hood to take bread to May. A sly guest met her in the wood and asked where she went. Dot held her paw to her lips. Her tail hid the bread bag. The troop had sent her with a quiz for spies. The guest got each guess wrong. At the feast, May gave him a cloth and wiped bits off his fur." },
  { id: "w5-074-the-pole-vault-picnic", title: "The pole vault picnic", pay: 16740, lib: 5, text: "Bo bends a pole to leap over a bar. His tail hooks a flag, and he flies into the snack tent. The troop runs to see if he is hurt. Bo sits in a bowl of jelly with both paws full of buns. He asks for one more try. Dot moves the snack tent. Bo now asks if he can skip ahead to the medal meal." },
  { id: "w5-077-the-ski-hill-queue", title: "The ski hill queue", pay: 16740, lib: 5, text: "Ned puts wax on his skis. He races past the troop and over the hill. At the base he finds a long queue. No one can walk back up the slick snow. Ned has waxed the whole slope with his skis. Dot lends him a rope. He goes up the tree and uses his tail to haul each skier up. The prize is a broom." },
  { id: "w5-032-the-giant-boot-garden", title: "The giant boot garden", pay: 16740, lib: 5, text: "Gus sees a huge boot by the road. The troop fears its owner will crush their huts. Gus rubs mud from the toe with one paw. His tail hooks a lace. Seeds fall in his fur. No owner comes. They fill the boot with soil and plant peas. When the giant seeks his boot, Gus asks him to wait till the peas are ripe." },
  { id: "w5-062-the-boat-race-anchor", title: "The boat race anchor", pay: 16740, lib: 5, text: "Ned rows hard, but his boat does not move. The troop calls out hints from the bank. He pulls with both paws and wraps his tail round the seat. Dot dives in to look. A rope holds the boat to a tree. Ned frees it and races ahead. He wins the race, then comes back for his lunch, which still hangs from the tree." },
  { id: "w5-072-the-table-tennis-sneeze", title: "The table tennis sneeze", pay: 16740, lib: 5, text: "May hits a tiny ball. Ned blows it back with a loud snort. The troop calls foul. Ned says his nose is a kind of bat. Dot reads the rules and finds no ban on noses. May puts dust on the ball. Ned gives a snort so hard the table slips away. The judge lets him keep his nose, but asks him to use a clean bat." },
  { id: "w5-021-the-spell-check-fairy", title: "The spell check fairy", pay: 16740, lib: 5, text: "Ivy cast a spell to make Pip bold. She said cold in error. Frost grew on his fur. His tail stuck to a rail. The troop got hot soup while Ivy tried again. She said gold. Pip shone, but still shook. He held his paw over her mouth and asked for a coat. Ivy gave him one. He faced the dark wood in warm plaid." },
  { id: "w5-122-the-wand-with-a-leash", title: "The wand with a leash", pay: 17010, lib: 5, text: "Bo lost his wand each day. Ivy tied it to his paw with a cord. At class he cast a spell to make it fly. The wand rose and took Bo with it. The troop held his tail. Bo hung over the desk till Ivy broke the spell. She tied the wand to the desk next time. Now Bo takes his desk to every class." },
  { id: "w5-068-the-pool-lane-dispute", title: "The pool lane dispute", pay: 17010, lib: 5, text: "Gus and Bo race in the pool. Gus wins, but Bo says his tail hit the line first. The troop reads the rules. They say first paw wins. Dot lays a plank over the pool. Gus walks over it on his paws. Bo swims below it. Gus wins again. The judge adds one word to the rules, and the plank is now a swim ramp." },
  { id: "w5-020-the-pillow-shield", title: "The pillow shield", pay: 17010, lib: 5, text: "Gus held a soft pad to block each blow. The troop sent him to face a stern guard. His tail shook, and his fur stood up. The guard swung a staff. The staff tore the pad and sent fluff out. Fluff flew past his paw. The guard had to snort so hard he lost the gate key. Gus came home with the key and a flat pad." },
  { id: "w5-073-the-clock-that-lied", title: "The clock that lied", pay: 17010, lib: 5, text: "The troop says Pip stole a plum at noon. The clock stood at noon when the plum was lost. Pip says he was at the pond. Dot opens the clock and finds a plum pit in its gears. The chef used the clock as a bin. Its hands have been stuck for days. Pip goes home with his name clear and a job to clean the clock." },
  { id: "w5-133-the-pirate-fruit-treaty", title: "The pirate fruit treaty", pay: 17010, lib: 5, text: "Bo and Gus both took the same isle. Both crews met on the beach. Dot drew a line down the sand. Bo got the trees, and Gus got the brook. Gus got fish, but Bo had no water for fruit. They gave one cup for one plum. At dusk the tide took the line away. They kept the trade since both liked their meal." },
  { id: "w5-096-the-fishing-line-race", title: "The fishing line race", pay: 17010, lib: 5, text: "Gus hooks a huge fish. He pulls so hard his tail grips the bank. The troop helps. At last a boot comes out of the lake. Dot reads a tag in it. Pip says he lost that boot last week. Gus says he still wins the best catch. Pip says the boot must go on a scale. He takes out the huge stone he hid in it." },
  { id: "w5-047-the-knight-of-the-leaf", title: "The knight of the leaf", pay: 17010, lib: 5, text: "Bo wears a leaf as his badge. He tells the troop that he will fear no storm. His fur is dry and his tail is high. The first gust rips the leaf away. Bo grabs it with one paw and folds it into a boat. He sets it in the ditch. Now he is lord of the fleet, and the storm gives him free wind." },
  { id: "w5-060-the-wrong-finish-tape", title: "The wrong finish tape", pay: 17010, lib: 5, text: "May runs past the red tape with a cheer. The troop gives a cheer too. Gus asks why she is in his yard. The tape marks his new paint. May has red lines in her fur. She looks down the road and sees the true goal. She runs there. The judge gives her a prize for best lines, while Gus hangs wet paint signs high up." },
  { id: "w5-019-the-royal-tax-on-rain", title: "The royal tax on rain", pay: 17010, lib: 5, text: "Rex taxed each drop of rain. The troop set jars out to count the debt. Pip kept his tail dry, but his fur got wet. He took one paw full of rain to the king. Rex asked for the fee. Pip asked for a slip for each drop. By noon Rex had no ink left. He made rain free and put a tax on ink." },
  { id: "w5-107-the-slow-light-beam", title: "The slow light beam", pay: 17010, lib: 5, text: "Ned built a beam to send fruit to the moon. The troop stood by to test it. He put a plum in the beam. The plum shone, then fell off the stand. That was all it did. Dot read the box. Ned had paid for a lamp. He kept it to light his desk and sent the plum by mail. It got there far less shiny." },
  { id: "w5-127-the-moon-cheese-lease", title: "The moon cheese lease", pay: 17010, lib: 5, text: "Gus went to the moon to get Swiss. The troop took bread. Gus found only stone, but he had told them to leave the Swiss at home. Dot set a slice of rock on her bread and took a fake bite. Gus asked how it was. Dot said it could use salt. They went home, where Gus had to buy Swiss for each empty slice." },
  { id: "w5-136-the-sea-monster-menu", title: "The sea monster menu", pay: 17010, lib: 5, text: "The troop saw a huge fin near the ship. Gus held out a fish to make peace. The fin went away, then came back with a card. It had a menu on it. Dot read that the fin was a sign for a cafe below the sea. Gus asked for lunch. A net rose with hot fish in it, plus the fish Gus had sent to pay for his meal." },
  { id: "w5-156-the-mouse-in-the-audit", title: "The mouse in the audit", pay: 17010, lib: 5, text: "Dot found a hole in the files. Rex said the staff kept files badly. The troop swept each desk for the lost sums. Gus found a mouse at rest on torn paper. Dot put it in a box with a blank form. The mouse ate the form. Rex said the audit was now done. Dot wrote that the chief had let the sole clue eat the proof." },
  { id: "w5-097-the-password-sneeze", title: "The password sneeze", pay: 17010, lib: 5, text: "Dot needs a code word to enter the club. She hears Gus snort at the door. The troop lets him in. Dot gives a snort too, but gets no reply. She peers in the lock hole. Gus has dust in his fur from the attic. The guard knows he found the lost games. Dot gets a game and gets in with a clean nose and dry lips." },
  { id: "w5-151-the-memo-about-memos", title: "The memo about memos", pay: 17010, lib: 5, text: "Rex sent a memo to ban memos. Dot sent a reply to ask if notes back were still fine. The troop got both and sent kind notes. By noon Rex had a desk full of notes. He gave a talk to clear it up. Gus wrote the talk down and sent it to each desk. Rex put his tail over the inbox and went out for tea." },
  { id: "w5-076-the-chalk-clue", title: "The chalk clue", pay: 17010, lib: 5, text: "Dot finds white dust on the floor. A cake is gone, so she tests each paw for chalk. The troop lines up. Bo has white fur and must go first. Dot tries one speck. It is flour. She goes to the oven and finds the cake still there. Bo asks her to say sorry. Dot gives him the first slice and a clean class slate." },
  { id: "w5-091-the-rugby-ball-nest", title: "The rugby ball nest", pay: 17010, lib: 5, text: "Bo sees an odd egg on the field. He puts it in his fur to keep it warm. The troop hunts for their ball. Dot asks Bo what he found. He shows her the egg. She says it is their rugby ball. Bo will give it back if they do not drop it. The whole game is now a very soft game of catch." },
  { id: "w5-116-the-sea-chest-lock", title: "The sea chest lock", pay: 17010, lib: 5, text: "Dot found a chest with seven locks. The troop tried seven keys. None fit. Bo held it up to shake it. The base fell off, and coins fell out. Dot saw that the locks were just glued to the lid. But the gold was real. Bo put each coin back and tied the chest shut with rope. No one could find the knot again." },
  { id: "w5-126-the-spellbook-lunchbox", title: "The spellbook lunchbox", pay: 17010, lib: 5, text: "Ivy gave Pip a book he must not open till noon. Pip put it in his lunch box. At noon he took it out and found jam on each page. The troop tried to read the words, but each word ran into the next. Pip cast one and made a huge loaf. Ivy kept the book. It was now the best lunch text in class." },
  { id: "w5-044-the-queen-of-moss", title: "The queen of moss", pay: 17010, lib: 5, text: "Ivy makes a crown from moss. It grows down her fur and round her tail. Soon she can just lift a paw. The troop soaks her each day. She asks them to stop, but they think it is royal music. Dot hears the words and cuts the moss. Ivy is free. The troop keeps the crown on a stump, where its reign is far less noisy." },
  { id: "w5-056-the-last-lap-snack", title: "The last lap snack", pay: 17010, lib: 5, text: "Gus leads the race till the last lap. He sees a fruit stall and stops for lunch. The troop races past. Gus asks the chef to pack his meal in a paper cone. He uses his tail to hold it as he runs. At the line he is last, but all the rest want a bite. He gives out bites in trade for each prize bow." },
  { id: "w5-140-the-pirate-flag-seamstress", title: "The pirate flag seamstress", pay: 17010, lib: 5, text: "May sewed a skull on her flag. She hoped the troop would seem scary. The skull had a grin by error. Each ship waved and came close for tea. May tried to sew a frown. Her tail shook, and the skull got one shut eye. She gave up and made the ship a cafe. The happy flag got more gold than any raid had done all year." },
  { id: "w5-202-the-sheriff-badge-polish", title: "The sheriff badge polish", pay: 17010, lib: 5, text: "Pip wears a badge so shiny the town shuts its eyes. The troop asks him to dull it. Pip says a law chief must shine. Dot puts mud on the badge. Pip wipes it off at once. A thief rides past while he buffs it. Pip sees the thief in the badge and gives chase. He keeps a small muddy spot on it for his next case." },
  { id: "w5-094-the-badminton-shade", title: "The badminton shade", pay: 17010, lib: 5, text: "Ivy hits a cork with a plume into a stiff wind. It lands in a tree. The troop calls for a new serve. Ivy looks up and sees six more corks on the same limb. She puts her tail round the trunk and gives it a shake. All seven fall onto the court. Dot hits them back one at a time. The troop plans to play under a roof next week." },
  { id: "w5-017-the-glass-gets-a-day-off", title: "The glass gets a day off", pay: 17280, lib: 5, text: "Rex asked his glass who was best. The glass said Dot. Rex wiped his fur and tried again. It said Dot once more. He hid his tail and hit the floor. The troop came to see the fuss. Dot stood right in front of the glass. Rex moved her aside. The glass said it could see a wall now, and the wall was quite nice." },
  { id: "w5-114-the-parrot-clerk", title: "The parrot clerk", pay: 17280, lib: 5, text: "Ned had a bird that spoke each word he said. The troop loved it till Ned named the spot where he hid his gold. The bird told the whole port. Ned wrote a false place on a card and told the bird to read it aloud. The bird said read it aloud. It knew the trick. Ned paid it one seed to keep each hint for a day." },
  { id: "w5-163-the-tail-on-the-witness-stand", title: "The tail on the witness stand", pay: 17280, lib: 5, text: "May swore to tell the truth. Her tail wound round the court chair. The judge asked if she saw Rex take the pie. May said she saw a red hat. The troop all wore red hats that day. Dot held up the pie tin. May sent her tail to the tin. The judge let her eyes rest and asked her tail to state its case." },
  { id: "w5-181-the-empty-suggestion-box", title: "The empty suggestion box", pay: 17280, lib: 5, text: "May asked the troop for ideas. She put a box by the door. No notes came in. Dot saw that the slot was too short for notes. May said the box was fine since no one said it was not. Dot put a coin in the slot. May tried to get it out and broke the box. Dot wrote make a wide slot on the new lid." },
  { id: "w5-063-the-missing-chess-king", title: "The missing chess king", pay: 17280, lib: 5, text: "Bo finds his king gone from the board. The troop looks under the rug. Dot spots a tiny crown in his fur. His tail had swept the king off the board and into his hood. Bo puts it back. Ned says the move is wrong. Bo nods and puts the king in his hood. From there it rules a warm realm with no foes in sight." },
  { id: "w5-093-the-trophy-that-rang", title: "The trophy that rang", pay: 17280, lib: 5, text: "Rex can not find his cup after the race. The troop looks in each bag. Dot hears a ring from the shed. Pip has hung the cup from a rope to call the troop for lunch. Rex asks for it back. Pip gives it to him. Now Rex hears a ring each time he moves his paw. He finds the lost spoon still tied in the cup." },
  { id: "w5-135-the-lost-space-parking-ticket", title: "The lost space parking ticket", pay: 17280, lib: 5, text: "Pip left his ship on a small rock. He came back with his troop and found a fine on the door. The fee was one moon stone. Pip chose a small rock to pay. Dot said he could not take the rock his ship sat on. Pip gave the guard his stone stud. The guard took it, and Pip held his shirt shut all the way home." },
  { id: "w5-176-the-meeting-room-booking", title: "The meeting room booking", pay: 17280, lib: 5, text: "Dot got a room for the troop. Rex got the same room for his wet hat. Dot put the hat on a chair and began the talk. Rex came in to claim his slot. The hat sat at the head of the table. The troop made it chair. It gave no long talks and cast a fine shade over the pie. Rex asked to join its team." },
  { id: "w5-006-the-slow-race-notice", title: "The slow race notice", pay: 17280, lib: 5, text: "Bo raced a snail to the gate. He ran so fast his fur blew back and his tail flew high. The troop gave a cheer. Bo put one paw on the gate and took the prize. The snail gave him the race rules. They had to reach their own home next. Bo had a long way left to run. The snail had its own home and won." },
  { id: "w5-082-the-silent-bell-case", title: "The silent bell case", pay: 17280, lib: 5, text: "The bell does not ring at noon. Dot asks each one in the troop where they were. Pip says he was in the bell tower. He hoped for a quiet nap, so he put wool in the bell. Dot pulls out the wool with one paw. The bell rings. Pip sits up in alarm. Dot puts the wool in a sack and gives it to him." },
  { id: "w5-212-the-wanted-poster-typo", title: "The wanted poster typo", pay: 17280, lib: 5, text: "A sign calls Pip a bread thief. The troop spots him by the bread shop. Dot asks why his face is on the wall. Pip reads the sign. The baker meant to call him bread chief. One word is wrong. Dot makes a new sign. Pip gets the job but still wears a mask. Flour dust makes him look a lot worse than the face on his old sign." },
  { id: "w5-081-the-limbo-judge", title: "The limbo judge", pay: 17280, lib: 5, text: "Bo bends under a low bar. His tail hits it. The troop says he lost. Bo asks if the tail rule is in print. Dot gives him the rules. He folds the page into a tube and uses it as a new bar. Now his tail can brush it with no harm. Dot bends under it once and takes the prize cup while Bo reads the rules." },
  { id: "w5-111-the-treasure-hammock", title: "The treasure hammock", pay: 17280, lib: 5, text: "Bo dug for gold on an isle. His troop dug till the pit was deep. Dot found a cloth chest at the base. It held a net and two hooks. Bo was sad till Dot hung the net in a tree. It made a fine bed. Bo lay in it and told the troop to dig some more. They put dirt in the pit and went for a swim." },
  { id: "w5-149-the-pirate-tide-alarm", title: "The pirate tide alarm", pay: 17280, lib: 5, text: "Gus tied a bell to the dock to warn of high tide. The troop heard it ring all night. At dawn Dot saw a crab pull its rope. Gus freed the rope and let the crab go. The tide rose with no sound, and the ship blew out. Dot gave the crab a job to ring the bell only at noon. It rang when he got lunch." },
  { id: "w5-169-the-getaway-cart-permit", title: "The getaway cart permit", pay: 17280, lib: 5, text: "Dot chose to flee fast in a cart. Ned asked for a pass to park it by the vault. She wrote out the form while the troop took the gold. The guard put his seal on it and gave her a spot far down the hill. Dot moved the cart. The troop went out with the gold at noon, in a legal march led by a cart with a pass." },
  { id: "w5-175-the-office-cactus-promotion", title: "The office cactus promotion", pay: 17280, lib: 5, text: "Ned gave a prize to the one who asked least. The troop had a row over the prize. Dot chose the plant by the door. It had asked none. Ned gave it a gold badge and its own desk. The plant asked for a large pot. The troop gazed at it. Gus came out from under the desk with a hose and said the new chief could use water." },
  { id: "w5-230-the-love-poem-meter", title: "The love poem meter", pay: 17280, lib: 5, text: "Ned sends a poem for Dot. Each line ends with love. The troop says it needs rhyme. Ned swaps every last word to dove. Dot reads it and asks where all the birds came from. Ned goes to buy a dove as proof. The bird eats his poem. Dot likes the bird more than the verse, and Ned asks it to write his next love note." },
  { id: "w5-023-the-goose-accountant", title: "The goose accountant", pay: 17280, lib: 5, text: "May owned a goose that laid gold eggs. She got a grand nest for it. The troop came to see her gold. May wiped her fur and held up an egg in one paw. Her tail swept a pile of bills. The nest cost more than the eggs. She sold the nest and got straw. The goose liked that, and May could at last pay for toast." },
  { id: "w5-115-the-plank-contest", title: "The plank contest", pay: 17280, lib: 5, text: "Gus told Pip to walk the plank. Pip put his tail round the rail and made the plank into a slide. The troop gave a clap. Gus tried the slide too and fell into the sea. Pip used the plank to pull him out. Gus asked for one more turn. The ship sat in port all day while each crew mate tried to land feet first." },
  { id: "w5-187-the-court-lunch-recess", title: "The court lunch recess", pay: 17280, lib: 5, text: "The judge said take a break. The troop ran to the yard to play. The judge meant a pause to read the file. Dot found him by the glass door as he eyed their game. He asked what the score was. Dot said tied. The judge took a bat and hit a home run. They came back to court with a clear score and mud on the case file." },
  { id: "w5-131-the-ship-in-the-bottle", title: "The ship in the bottle", pay: 17280, lib: 5, text: "Rex put a tiny ship in a glass flask. Then he cast a spell to make his troop fit in it. They went round the cork and had no way out. Dot used her tail to haul the mast up. The mast poked the cork out. They all grew big again. Rex kept the flask as a vase. Dot put a large rose in it to block the port." },
  { id: "w5-009-the-tower-delivery", title: "The tower delivery", pay: 17280, lib: 5, text: "May lived in a tall tower. She let her tail hang down so Gus could climb. He had a cake in one paw. Bits got in her fur, and the cake fell on the troop below. May went down to taste it. Gus gazed at the open door. All week he had come up by the wall. The door had been for cake carts all along." },
  { id: "w5-022-the-moat-lesson", title: "The moat lesson", pay: 17280, lib: 5, text: "Ned dug a moat to keep pals out. Soon his troop could not get in for lunch. He waved a paw from the wall. His tail sank and his fur smelt of mud. Dot tied a rope to a cart full of pals and threw Ned the loose end. Ned drew so hard the cart flew over the moat. He had pals at last, all in his soup." },
  { id: "w5-120-the-gold-tooth-route", title: "The gold tooth route", pay: 17280, lib: 5, text: "Pip hid a coin under a loose tooth. No thief would look there. At lunch he bit a hard nut, and the tooth came out. The troop ran round the deck to find it. Dot found a nut with a coin in it. Pip had spat the coin into its shell. He put the coin in a pouch and let the tooth lie under his soft bed for a fair trade." },
  { id: "w5-041-the-fairy-census", title: "The fairy census", pay: 17280, lib: 5, text: "Dot hears a voice in a rose. It asks for milk. She sets a cup by the rose. Next day ten cups stand on the step. The troop helps her fill them. Dot gets milk on her fur, tail, and paw. She asks how many fair folk live there. One voice says one. It has ten tiny cats. Dot sets out a cow and goes back to bed." },
  { id: "w5-117-the-captain-hat-tax", title: "The captain hat tax", pay: 17280, lib: 5, text: "Rex wore the high hat on the ship. He said that made him boss. The troop piled hats on their heads to claim his rank. Dot came with no hat at all. She could see under the sail, so she held the wheel while the rest hit the rails. Rex gave her the wheel. She sold the hats to buy a chart of small reefs." },
  { id: "w5-118-the-anchor-garden", title: "The anchor garden", pay: 17280, lib: 5, text: "The troop could not lift the iron hook. Gus drew the rope, but it was taut. Dot went down to look. Roots had grown round the iron. The ship had sat in port for weeks. Bo got a saw and freed it. Gus held up the iron hook with green vines on it. He set sail at last, with tiny vines hung on the bow." },
  { id: "w5-161-the-fax-jungle", title: "The fax jungle", pay: 17280, lib: 5, text: "Bo sent a fax to the next room. The troop heard a grind, then saw paper climb the wall. Bo had fed the fax a long roll. Dot took its tail end and tore it free. The fax had split hello into five parts and put one part on each page. Rex put all five pages on the wall as proof that his firm used less paper." },
  { id: "w5-098-the-skating-rink-thaw", title: "The skating rink thaw", pay: 17280, lib: 5, text: "Ned makes a rink in his yard. The troop has steel on each shoe. They wait for the judge. The sun rises, and the rink melts. Dot finds a pair of shoes. She puts them on and leaps into the pool. Ned calls it a new sport. They award her a medal for best leap. The judge comes dry and goes home with mud up to his knees." },
  { id: "w5-157-the-daily-standup", title: "The daily standup", pay: 17280, lib: 5, text: "The troop stood for a daily work chat. Rex said no one could sit till each task was clear. Pip asked what his task was. Rex said to state his task. Dot asked who chose it. Rex said they would talk of that next week. Gus put seats under each tail. The troop sat at once. Rex named it a bold pilot and made a new chart." },
  { id: "w5-179-the-team-building-raft", title: "The team building raft", pay: 17280, lib: 5, text: "Rex asked the troop to build a raft from junk. Dot tied seats to a desk. Gus added the clock. May put the files on top. The raft could float. Rex asked what they knew now. Dot said their work place made a fine boat. They set sail while Rex ran along the bank. He held the task list and asked them to come back for a talk." },
  { id: "w5-119-the-ghost-ship-laundry", title: "The ghost ship laundry", pay: 17280, lib: 5, text: "May saw white forms move on a dark ship. The troop hid below deck. May took a lamp on board. The forms were wet coats on a line. Wind blew them up as if alive. She found Ned as he tried to fold them. May used her tail to hold the line still. The troop came back, and each got a clean shirt in place of a scary tale." },
  { id: "w5-141-the-spell-that-swept-names", title: "The spell that swept names", pay: 17280, lib: 5, text: "Bo cast a spell to clean the class list. It took each name right off. The troop could not reply at roll call. Ivy asked Bo who he was. He did not know. Dot found the names in a dust pan. She put them back by size. Bo was Gus for one day. He liked the large lunch, but Gus asked for his small boots back." },
  { id: "w5-216-the-action-hero-lunch-break", title: "The action hero lunch break", pay: 17280, lib: 5, text: "Pip has ten ticks to stop a loud alarm. The troop eyes the clock. He leaps over boxes and slips under a gate. Dot uses the open side door. She turns off the alarm and puts lunch on the table. Pip comes in with torn pants and a grand pose. Dot asks him to carry the soup. He says his knees need a stunt aide for that scene." },
  { id: "w5-164-the-lawyer-who-billed-silence", title: "The lawyer who billed silence", pay: 17550, lib: 5, text: "Ned said he could win the case with one word. Pip paid him a coin for each pause in court. Ned sat quiet. The troop saw the judge wait. At last Dot said yes. Ned stood and said no. He had used his one word. The judge asked him for proof. Ned said his one word was used up and sent Pip a bill for the pause." },
  { id: "w5-168-the-decoy-decoy", title: "The decoy decoy", pay: 17550, lib: 5, text: "Pip hired Rex as a decoy for the gem theft. Rex hired Gus to play the decoy in his place. Gus sent May, who sent a doll. The troop put the doll by the gate. The guard held it and asked for its name. Pip took the gem. He then had to steal the doll too, since it held all the keys in its tiny felt paw." },
  { id: "w5-178-the-legal-dictionary-dinner", title: "The legal dictionary dinner", pay: 17550, lib: 5, text: "Gus spoke in court with a book of long words. The judge asked what he meant. Gus read a word twice as long. The troop slept on the bench. Dot took the book and asked Gus to use words he used at home. Gus said pie. The judge knew that at once. He split the pie in half and used the book as a tray for both sides." },
  { id: "w5-200-the-court-sketch-artist", title: "The court sketch artist", pay: 17550, lib: 5, text: "May drew the judge for the news. The troop saw a stern face with huge ears. The judge said the image was wrong. May made the ears small. He still said no. Dot asked what he liked. He asked to look pure. May put a halo on his head. The troop had a good laugh. The judge ruled that he was less pure with a hoop over his head." },
  { id: "w5-170-the-locksmith-souvenir", title: "The locksmith souvenir", pay: 17550, lib: 5, text: "Gus could open any lock. The troop paid him to open a safe. He did it in one try and took the key as his fee. Dot asked why he kept it. Gus said he had a box of keys at home. He could not open that box. The troop gave him a new box with no lock, and Gus gave back the fee to pay for it." },
  { id: "w5-210-the-horse-parking-ticket", title: "The horse parking ticket", pay: 17550, lib: 5, text: "Bo ties his horse by the bank. Ned puts a fine on its mane. The troop asks what rule it broke. Ned says the horse took two white spots. Dot tests the spots with a rope. One is just large for a hat. Bo puts his hat there and keeps the horse in the other one. Ned asks the hat for rent, and Dot calls for a new mayor." },
  { id: "w5-067-the-muddy-alibi", title: "The muddy alibi", pay: 17550, lib: 5, text: "Ned says he was out in the rain when the cake was lost. His fur is full of mud. Dot puts one paw in the mud. It is warm and has a sweet scent. The troop sees Ned lick his cuff. He used cake mix to fake the rain. Dot leads him to the bath. Now he has a real need to be wet and no cake." },
  { id: "w5-030-the-door-with-tests", title: "The door with tests", pay: 17550, lib: 5, text: "Bo keeps a door that gives a quiz. Pip knows the right reply, but the door tests him. Pip rubs his fur and wraps his tail round the knob. The troop waits in the rain. Bo puts his paw on a hinge and asks the door to state its proof. The door has none. Bo gives it a book to study. It opens to let him turn each page." },
  { id: "w5-085-the-slow-bike-medal", title: "The slow bike medal", pay: 17550, lib: 5, text: "Pip rides hard with his tail round the seat. He goes past the troop, but his wheel comes off. He hauls the bike to the goal on his back. The judge says he must ride it. Pip sits on it and asks Dot for a push. She gives him a push over the line. He wins last place and gives Dot the bell from his old bike." },
  { id: "w5-090-the-disappearing-clue", title: "The disappearing clue", pay: 17550, lib: 5, text: "Dot cuts a clue in ice to keep it fresh. The troop goes with her to the crime scene. The ice melts in her paw. Now she has no clue and a wet map. Pip asks what the clue said. Dot says it said keep cool. The lost cake was in the cold room all along. She puts her next note on paper and keeps it dry." },
  { id: "w5-087-the-hoop-in-the-tree", title: "The hoop in the tree", pay: 17550, lib: 5, text: "Gus puts a hoop high in a tree. The troop lobs balls but can not score. Dot goes up and finds a nest in the hoop. She moves the nest to a safe limb and drops the hoop. Gus says the game is too easy now. Dot puts him in the nest. He must keep each ball out. By dusk he asks to join the team on the grass." },
  { id: "w5-099-the-library-card-chase", title: "The library card chase", pay: 17550, lib: 5, text: "Pip loses his card in the book room. Dot asks where he last used it. Pip says at lunch. The troop goes to the cafe and sees the card under a short table leg. It makes the table level. Dot pulls it out. Soup tips out. Pip gives it back and pays cash for his next book. The clerk gives him a card with four tiny legs." },
  { id: "w5-162-the-court-of-crumbs", title: "The court of crumbs", pay: 17550, lib: 5, text: "Pip sued Gus for the last slice of cake. The judge asked for proof. Dot held up a crumb. Gus said a crumb could come from any cake. The troop gave a nod. Dot asked Gus to open his mouth. He had blue icing on his teeth. Gus said that meant only that he liked blue. The judge told both sides to bring whole cakes for a fair test." },
  { id: "w5-215-the-silver-spur-alarm", title: "The silver spur alarm", pay: 17550, lib: 5, text: "Ned wears loud spurs to scare a thief. The troop hears him come from miles away. A thief hides each time the spurs ring. Dot wraps them in cloth. Ned grabs the thief. No one hears him come back. He rings a spoon on his badge. The town comes out to cheer. Dot takes the spoon back and asks him to wash the spurs while she makes soup." },
  { id: "w5-235-the-dance-card-auction", title: "The dance card auction", pay: 17550, lib: 5, text: "May puts names on a dance card. Rex buys it as a list of debts. He asks each one in the troop for a coin. Dot reads the card and takes his paw. They dance till Rex is dizzy. May says he must dance five times more. Rex gives the card back for free and asks to sit down. Dot puts his last coin in the music box." },
  { id: "w5-066-the-golf-hole-thief", title: "The golf hole thief", pay: 17550, lib: 5, text: "Rex hits a ball at the hole. It rolls out each time. The troop looks on as he tries again. Dot bends to look into the hole. Pip has put his tail in it to keep worms warm. Rex asks him to move. Pip lifts his tail, and six balls fall in at once. Rex marks six wins on his card. Dot takes away his pen." },
  { id: "w5-088-the-lunch-bell-thief", title: "The lunch bell thief", pay: 17550, lib: 5, text: "The lunch bell is gone. The troop waits at their desks with empty bowls. Dot sees Ned wave both paws at the cook. He has tied the bell to his tail. Each wag rings it, but the thick door stops the sound. Dot opens the door. The cook comes with soup. Ned tries to sit down, and the bell calls for lunch all over again." },
  { id: "w5-109-the-rocket-salad", title: "The rocket salad", pay: 17550, lib: 5, text: "May put green fuel in her ship. It would not rise. The troop had a look in the tank and found pea soup. Gus had used the fuel jar as a lunch pot. May took out the soup with a cup. Gus gave her the real fuel from his lunch flask. The ship rose at once. Gus sat by each bowl to check it prior to tea time." },
  { id: "w5-139-the-star-chart-stain", title: "The star chart stain", pay: 17550, lib: 5, text: "Ned spilt soup on the star chart. The troop had to steer by the red dots. Each dot led them to the same old world. Dot tried one. It was a red bean. Ned wiped the chart and found the true path below. The ship got home at last. Dot made a fresh chart on a plate and told Ned that he could eat those stars at home." },
  { id: "w5-196-the-official-lunch-count", title: "The official lunch count", pay: 17550, lib: 5, text: "May used the lunch count to see who came to work. Gus took two bowls and wore a new hat for the next count. May put his name down twice. Dot asked why the firm had more staff than desks. Gus put one bowl on the floor. May gave the floor a staff badge. It was never late and never asked for leave. Gus kept its lunch." },
  { id: "w5-070-the-tug-rope-knot", title: "The tug rope knot", pay: 17550, lib: 5, text: "The troop makes two teams to play tug. Pip ties his tail to the rope for more grip. Dot tells him to use his paws. He says his plan is smart. Each team pulls. Pip flies up and lands on a low limb. His tail holds the rope there as both teams let go. The game ends as a swing game, and Pip needs the first push." },
  { id: "w5-137-the-rocket-countdown-nap", title: "The rocket countdown nap", pay: 17550, lib: 5, text: "Rex set a timer for lift. The troop saw the timer count down. At zero, a bell rang, but the ship did not move. Rex had used his nap timer. Dot asked where the real ship key was. Rex had it under his bed. He went to bed to fetch it and fell into sleep. The troop flew at last with their chief snug in his bunk." },
  { id: "w5-075-the-lost-library-hush", title: "The lost library hush", pay: 17550, lib: 5, text: "Dot hears a faint chirp in the book room. The troop can not read in peace. She looks on each shelf and finds no one. May shows her the sign that says hush. A toy wheel turns at its back when the wind blows. Dot shuts the pane. The sound stops. Then the room gets hot. The troop opens the pane and reads books about noisy gears." },
  { id: "w5-155-the-remote-work-vine", title: "The remote work vine", pay: 17550, lib: 5, text: "Bo asked to work from a tree. Ned said yes if he could still reach the staff. Bo ran a vine from the tree to each desk. The troop gave tugs to send news. A hard tug drew Ned out of his chair. Bo wrote it down as a plea for help. Ned let him stay in the tree but asked that all new notes come by paper plane." },
  { id: "w5-129-the-fairy-chalkboard", title: "The fairy chalkboard", pay: 17820, lib: 5, text: "Bo wrote a spell on the class slate. The words slid off and ran out the door. The troop ran after them into the yard. Ivy told Bo to write a stop spell. He wrote stop, and the words lined up by the fence. Bo used them to spell out lunch. Ivy gave a sigh and let the class eat while she swept the last word off the path." },
  { id: "w5-144-the-magic-hat-filing-cabinet", title: "The magic hat filing cabinet", pay: 17820, lib: 5, text: "Pip put all his class notes in a magic hat. He asked for his sums, and a hare came out. He asked for his magic, and got a new hare. The troop found a whole class of hares in the hat. They had used his notes for their desks. Pip gave them roots in trade. They gave back his work with red marks where he had got each sum wrong." },
  { id: "w5-220-the-explosion-countdown-clock", title: "The explosion countdown clock", pay: 17820, lib: 5, text: "Rex sets a timer to scare the troop in a drill. Pip runs in to cut a wire. Dot reads the label. It is an egg timer. Rex says he meant to test their nerve. The timer rings, and Gus comes with eggs. Pip holds the cut wire. His eggs are cold since he cut the stove wire. Dot gives him an egg and asks for the wire back." },
  { id: "w5-138-the-invisible-ink-test", title: "The invisible ink test", pay: 17820, lib: 5, text: "Dot wrote all her work in ink no one could see. Ivy held the page up to the light. It was blank. The troop said Dot must have won. Ivy gave her a prize no one could see. Dot felt the empty box with one paw. She asked for plain ink next time. Ivy gave her a real pen and kept the blank prize for the next test." },
  { id: "w5-199-the-case-of-the-printed-tail", title: "The case of the printed tail", pay: 17820, lib: 5, text: "A tail mark was on a memo. Dot asked the troop to line up. Rex said no. He was the boss. Dot held the memo up to his chair. The ink was the same as the seat. Rex had sat on the memo to hide it. Dot gave him a clear chair. He hid no more notes under it, but his hat soon grew very full and fell off." },
  { id: "w5-061-the-clue-in-the-ice", title: "The clue in the ice", pay: 17820, lib: 5, text: "Dot finds a key in a block of ice. The troop needs it to open the snack shed. She holds it near the fire. The ice melts, but the key melts to a thin curl. It was made of sugar. Pip says he froze it for a prank. Dot asks him to fetch the real key. It is in his hat. He now keeps all candy far from the fire." },
  { id: "w5-092-the-footprints-on-the-roof", title: "The footprints on the roof", pay: 17820, lib: 5, text: "Dot sees paw marks in a cake on the roof. No steps lead up the hut. The troop fears a thief with wings. Gus says he threw the cake up there to cool. Dot finds a pie fork stuck in it. Its five tips made the marks when Gus threw the cake. Gus gets his cake and Dot gets a slice for the clue to a crime with five metal toes." },
  { id: "w5-147-the-spell-for-neat-desks", title: "The spell for neat desks", pay: 17820, lib: 5, text: "Ivy cast a spell to make the desks neat. Each desk shut up to form a small cube. The troop had no place to sit. Bo put a cube in his paw and shook it. The desk rose up and threw his books. Ivy told the troop to give each cube a soft tap. They shut their desks after class and took the whole room home in their lunch bags." },
  { id: "w5-208-the-gold-rush-lunch", title: "The gold rush lunch", pay: 17820, lib: 5, text: "Rex finds a gold flake in the brook. The troop runs to pan for gold. Dot tries one flake and says it is corn. Gus has lost his lunch in the brook. Rex says corn can still be sold. The troop fills sacks and heads to town. Gus meets them with a bill for his lunch. The gold rush ends in a long talk about who owns the bits." },
  { id: "w5-221-the-secret-tunnel-tour", title: "The secret tunnel tour", pay: 17820, lib: 5, text: "Ned digs a shaft under the vault. The troop goes after him. At the end they find a sign for tours. Dot has made the shaft a tour stop. Ned says she broke the plan. Dot holds up the tour fees. They have made more than the vault holds. Ned fills the shaft in for a high price tour where each guest must guess what was once under the soil." },
  { id: "w5-065-the-locked-jam-jar", title: "The locked jam jar", pay: 17820, lib: 5, text: "May locks a jar of jam in a glass case. At dawn the jam is gone. Dot tests the lock and finds it sound. The troop fears magic. Dot finds a straw in a tiny hole in the case. It leads up to the roof. Gus sits there with a red paw and a full belly. May ties a bell to the straw. At his next sip, the whole troop comes for jam." },
  { id: "w5-183-the-contract-with-crumbs", title: "The contract with crumbs", pay: 17820, lib: 5, text: "Pip put his name on a deal at lunch. Jam stuck two pages shut. The troop read just the first page. Dot got them apart at dusk. The next page said Pip owed Gus a pie each week. Gus gave a grin. Dot held the page by the fire. More jam fell off. A third page fell out. It said Gus had to bake each pie. Gus got his apron." },
  { id: "w5-195-the-briefcase-maze", title: "The briefcase maze", pay: 17820, lib: 5, text: "Ned put his notes in a case in a case. He said that made them safe. At court the troop saw him open each lock. Dot asked for the key to the tiny case. Ned said it was in the large one. The judge took a break while they had a look. Dot found the notes on top of the first case. Ned had left them there to make a label." },
  { id: "w5-203-the-stagecoach-fare", title: "The stagecoach fare", pay: 17820, lib: 5, text: "Gus stops a coach to take its gold. The coach chief says the coach has only bills. The troop looks in the sacks. Each sack has rent bills. Gus tries to leave, but Dot says he made the coach stop and must pay the late fee. Gus hauls it to town on his own. He gets there with no gold and a new job as a horse with a hat." },
  { id: "w5-223-the-parachute-tablecloth", title: "The parachute tablecloth", pay: 17820, lib: 5, text: "Bo leaps from a tower with a cloth on his back. The troop gasps. Dot says it is her lunch cloth, not a chute. Bo lands in a cart of soft hay. He holds the cloth up as proof his plan won. Dot shows him the hay. Bo hires the cart for each new leap. His next stunt must wait since the cart is busy with hay for the cows." },
  { id: "w5-229-the-rose-allergy", title: "The rose allergy", pay: 17820, lib: 5, text: "Rex gives Ivy a rose at their first date. Her nose gives a blast and his hat blows off. The troop grabs it. Rex gets one more rose, but Ivy gives a snort again. Dot gives him a paper rose. Ivy grins and puts it in a vase. Rex asks why it is so much nicer. Ivy says it stays fresh and never makes her nose try to leave her face." },
  { id: "w5-064-the-race-on-poles", title: "The race on poles", pay: 17820, lib: 5, text: "Pip ties long poles to his feet to beat the tall troop in a race. He takes huge steps till a paw slips. He lands on his back while the poles run down the slope. Dot grabs them at the line. The judge says the poles win. Pip asks them to speak. They stay mute, so he takes the prize for them and buys a pair of flat shoes." },
  { id: "w5-159-the-tea-expense", title: "The tea expense", pay: 17820, lib: 5, text: "May paid for tea and filed a claim. Ned asked for proof. She gave him the bill. He asked who had drunk it. The troop held up their mugs. He asked if the tea aided work. Dot put cold tea on his stuck desk lock. It swung open. Ned let the claim pass as tool care and asked if they could fix his loud chair with bread." },
  { id: "w5-177-the-badge-reader-audit", title: "The badge reader audit", pay: 17820, lib: 5, text: "Pip got a badge to enter work. The gate would not let him in. He held it with his paw, then his tail. No luck. The troop waved from the glass door. Dot came out and read his badge. It said guest. Pip had done work there for years. Rex wrote old guest on it. Pip still had to knock each day to get past the gate." },
  { id: "w5-218-the-laser-maze-dust", title: "The laser maze dust", pay: 17820, lib: 5, text: "May faces a maze of red beams. The troop tells her to crawl. Dot sees dust in the air and asks for a broom. May uses the broom while Dot turns off each lamp. The beams fade. Rex comes in to test his new alarm and finds a very clean floor. He hires May to sweep. She gets a key to every vault and will never have to crawl again." },
  { id: "w5-167-the-bank-vault-fan", title: "The bank vault fan", pay: 17820, lib: 5, text: "Bo chose to steal a gem from a vault. His troop wore black and crept in. The alarm was quiet, but a loud fan blew their hats away. Dot ran for hers and hit the alarm lever. Bo asked why she let the plan fail. Dot said the hat was on loan. They left the gem and stole back only their own hats, then paid the bank a mop fee." },
  { id: "w5-245-the-box-of-chocolates-map", title: "The box of chocolates map", pay: 17820, lib: 5, text: "Rex gives Ivy a map in place of candy. She opens it and sees a trail. The troop goes to a tree, then a bench, then the cafe. Rex waits there with the candy. Ivy asks why he made her walk so far. Rex says he spent all his coins on candy and had none left for a cab. Dot hands him the fare for a bus and eats the first sweet." },
  { id: "w5-014-the-royal-nap-alarm", title: "The royal nap alarm", pay: 17820, lib: 5, text: "The troop said a spell had made Rex sleep for years. Pip went to wake him with a kiss, but found the whole troop at rest too. Fur lay on each chair. Tails hung from the lamps. Pip put his paw on a gong. He hit it once. Rex sat up and asked for tea. The spell had no power. The royal lunch had just been much too large." },
  { id: "w5-191-the-witness-clock", title: "The witness clock", pay: 18090, lib: 5, text: "Pip took a clock to court to prove the time of the theft. The judge asked it to speak. Dot wound the clock. It rang at noon. Pip said that was the time of the theft. The judge wound it again. It rang at noon once more. The troop gave a sigh. Pip took back the clock and gave the judge his lunch bell. Court ended early for soup." },
  { id: "w5-189-the-lease-on-the-desk", title: "The lease on the desk", pay: 18090, lib: 5, text: "Rex made the troop pay rent for each desk. They did work on their laps. Rex then asked rent for seats. Dot went up a tree and did work on a limb. Rex asked rent for the tree. Dot asked for proof he owned it. He went to fetch the deed. The troop moved to the next tree. They sent Rex a bill for shade while he read his deed." },
  { id: "w5-240-the-beach-proposal-shell", title: "The beach proposal shell", pay: 18090, lib: 5, text: "Gus puts a ring in a shell for Dot. The troop waits close by. A crab takes the shell and runs off. Gus runs after it down the beach. Dot looks on till he comes back with the crab in a pail. She opens the shell and finds the ring. The crab finds a new home in the empty ring box. Dot says yes to both the ring and the tiny guest." },
  { id: "w5-134-the-spell-for-spare-hands", title: "The spell for spare hands", pay: 18090, lib: 5, text: "May asked Ivy for extra hands to wash the bowls. Ivy gave her four. May held more bowls, but her cuffs did not fit. The troop gave her a huge coat. Each new hand got stuck in a pouch. May could not reach the bowls. She asked Ivy to take them back. Ivy left one spare hand to hold the towel while May had a wash in her old shirt." },
  { id: "w5-145-the-asteroid-ball-game", title: "The asteroid ball game", pay: 18090, lib: 5, text: "Rex hit a ball from one rock to the next. The troop stood ready to catch it. The ball went round the rocks and came back to Rex. He hit it again. Dot said he was alone in the game. Rex asked her to throw from the other side. Both balls hit the same net and stuck. The troop had to pull them free and start a new sport." },
  { id: "w5-143-the-treasure-island-picnic-tax", title: "The treasure island picnic tax", pay: 18090, lib: 5, text: "Ivy dug up a chest on the isle. The troop gave a cheer at the gold in it. Then they saw a bill for harm to the grass. Ivy owed more gold than she found. Dot put the grass back in the hole. The bill grew green and fell apart. Ivy kept the gold, but now she had to water the hole each day so the bill would stay small." },
  { id: "w5-173-the-elevator-alibi", title: "The elevator alibi", pay: 18090, lib: 5, text: "Pip used a lift ride as his alibi. He said he was mid ride when the coins were lost. Dot read the lift log. The troop had used it all day, but Pip had never hit a knob. He had been on the roof of the car. Dot found the coins under his tail. Pip said he was just there to hold them down so they would not roll." },
  { id: "w5-224-the-secret-code-dinner", title: "The secret code dinner", pay: 18090, lib: 5, text: "Pip says the code word is soup. The troop goes to the cafe to meet a spy. Each guest asks for soup, so Pip can not tell who is the spy. Dot asks who wants a fork with it. Rex lifts his paw. The real spy knows the next code is fork. Dot gives him a spoon to use. He must eat lunch till they can talk of the plan." },
  { id: "w5-130-the-telescope-queue", title: "The telescope queue", pay: 18090, lib: 5, text: "May set up a scope to view a rare star. The troop stood in line all night. Each guest saw one round light. At dawn Dot put her paw over the front. The light shone on. May had left the lens cap on, and a small lamp lit the glass from the back. The troop asked for coins back. May gave each one a turn to view a real star at night." },
  { id: "w5-142-the-space-elevator-button", title: "The space elevator button", pay: 18090, lib: 5, text: "Gus rode a lift up to the stars. The troop had hit each knob to see what it did. The lift had a stop at every cloud. Dot asked them to stop. Gus put his paw over the knobs, but his tail hit the one for down. They rode all the way home. Next time Dot gave the troop toy knobs and kept the real ones in her pouch." },
  { id: "w5-158-the-stolen-stapler-warrant", title: "The stolen stapler warrant", pay: 18090, lib: 5, text: "Ned lost his clip tool and sent Dot to the desk. She saw one bent pin in the rug. The troop kept quiet as she read the pin trail to Rex. His pants were full of them. He had used the clip tool to fix his hem. Dot took it back with a paw. Rex asked if he could keep the pins. His pants were now at risk." },
  { id: "w5-225-the-heroic-door-kick", title: "The heroic door kick", pay: 18090, lib: 5, text: "Gus kicks the door to burst into a room. It does not move. The troop asks him to try again. Dot reads the sign that says pull. Gus pulls, but the door still stays shut. Dot shows him the latch. Gus lifts it and gets in at last. Rex has left for lunch. Gus sits in the empty room and asks Dot to film his exit this time." },
  { id: "w5-079-the-ball-that-went-home", title: "The ball that went home", pay: 18090, lib: 5, text: "Pip hits a ball out of the park. The troop runs to fetch it. The ball rolls into a hole and stays there. Dot looks in and sees Bo at rest with it under his head. He used it as a soft bed last night and wrote his name on it. Pip buys a new ball. Bo asks him to sign a lease if he wants to use the old ball again." },
  { id: "w5-182-the-grant-for-a-ladder", title: "The grant for a ladder", pay: 18360, lib: 5, text: "Bo asked for steps to fix the roof. Rex said he must prove the roof was bad. Bo sent a photo from below. Rex asked for one from above. The troop made a stack of boxes. Bo went up with his phone. The stack fell, but he got his shot. Rex paid for the steps but said no to the bill for the boxes. Bo sent a photo of those too." },
  { id: "w5-185-the-open-door-policy", title: "The open door policy", pay: 18360, lib: 5, text: "Rex said his door was never shut. The troop went in to ask for more pay. Rex shut it at once. Dot took off the hinge pins to keep his word true. Wind blew his notes into the hall. Rex said he would pay more if she fixed the door. Dot put the pins back but kept the door wide open. The troop lined up for more pay." },
  { id: "w5-186-the-change-control-fan", title: "The change control fan", pay: 18360, lib: 5, text: "Gus asked to turn on a fan. Ned said each new step must have a form. Gus wrote it out while the troop got hot. Ned asked Dot to test the form. Dot used it as a fan and sent it round. The troop got cool. Ned said no new step was now due. Gus kept blank forms by each desk and put the fan away to make room for them." },
  { id: "w5-213-the-wagon-wheel-feud", title: "The wagon wheel feud", pay: 18360, lib: 5, text: "May and Bo fight over one wagon wheel. The troop can not solve the claim. Dot cuts the wheel in half. Both say no to their share. Dot says that shows they both care for the wheel. Gus says it shows a half wheel can not roll. Dot glues it back up and keeps it from both. She makes a swing with it and makes both sides pay for rides." },
  { id: "w5-231-the-cafe-seat-shuffle", title: "The cafe seat shuffle", pay: 18360, lib: 5, text: "Pip plans to meet May at a cafe. The troop has taken every seat. Dot moves them round so Pip can sit next to May. Gus ends up with three cakes, and Bo loses his soup. By the time Pip sits down, May has gone to pay. Dot moves the whole troop to the till. Pip and May meet there and go to a new cafe to eat in peace." },
  { id: "w5-194-the-boardroom-swing", title: "The boardroom swing", pay: 18360, lib: 5, text: "Rex used a swing as his chair. The troop had to push him while he spoke. Dot gave one hard push, and Rex flew out the door. He went on with his talk in the hall. The troop heard his voice grow faint. Dot said the talk was done. Rex came back at lunch and spoke well of their drive. He had to push his own swing after that." },
  { id: "w5-201-the-duel-at-five-past-noon", title: "The duel at five past noon", pay: 18360, lib: 5, text: "Rex asks Bo to meet at noon for a duel. The troop waits by the clock. Bo comes late by five ticks. Rex says the duel is void. Bo says the clock is fast. Dot takes both hats and asks them to fix the clock first. They climb the tower and find a loose gear. At noon next day they argue over who did more work, then go for lunch." },
  { id: "w5-246-the-love-song-rehearsal-fee", title: "The love song rehearsal fee", pay: 18360, lib: 5, text: "Ned hires Gus to teach him a love song. The troop hears him sing. Dot asks who the song is for. Ned says May. May comes in with a bill for the room they are using. She owns the music hall. Ned sings to pay his rent. May takes the song but bills him for the echo. Gus gives Ned a small song of just one verse to learn next time." },
  { id: "w5-180-the-quality-assurance-plum", title: "The quality assurance plum", pay: 18360, lib: 5, text: "Ned tried each plum to test its taste. He took one bite to see if it was ripe. The troop sent back each half eaten plum. Dot told Ned to use just one plum for the test. He did, but that plum was sour. He wrote sour on each crate and paid less for them all. Dot found him at lunch with sweet plums and no test log." },
  { id: "w5-184-the-false-safe-alarm", title: "The false safe alarm", pay: 18360, lib: 5, text: "Ned heard a click from the safe and ran. The troop fled with him. Dot had a look. It was a toy clock set for lunch. She took the gold and met Ned by the gate. Ned said he had saved them from a trap. Dot gave him the clock as his cut. He kept it shut all day for fear of the bell. It rang at lunch in spite of that." },
  { id: "w5-190-the-privacy-screen", title: "The privacy screen", pay: 18360, lib: 5, text: "May asked for a cloth to hide her work. Ned gave her one full of holes. The troop could read each note. Dot hung a coat over it. Ned said that was wrong. May wrote her next notes on the coat. Ned could not read the back, but wore it to see his boss. His boss saw May ask for more pay in huge red words all over his back." },
  { id: "w5-207-the-paper-deputy", title: "The paper deputy", pay: 18360, lib: 5, text: "Pip names Gus his aide. Gus asks for a badge. Pip has only one, so they share it on odd days. The troop takes cases on the wrong day. Dot draws a new badge on paper. Gus wears it with pride till rain turns it blue. Pip gives him the real one and wears the paper badge. In the next storm he sits under a tree. He gives out soggy notes." },
  { id: "w5-248-the-ring-size-chart", title: "The ring size chart", pay: 18360, lib: 5, text: "Pip asks May for her ring size. She feels he means the show ring where she works. The troop helps him gauge it. Pip buys a hoop as wide as a hut. He bends a knee to offer it. May grins and uses it for her next show. Dot gives Pip a tiny ring to try again. May says yes, but asks that the big one stay since it earns their rent." },
  { id: "w5-150-the-magic-graduation-robe", title: "The magic graduation robe", pay: 18360, lib: 5, text: "Bo wore a robe that grew as he did. At the class feast he ate three cakes. The robe grew right over the hall. The troop fell over its hem. Ivy asked him to stand up. Bo could not find the cuffs. Dot cut a hole in the top, and Bo poked his head out. The robe was now the feast tent, and Bo sat in it till wash day." },
  { id: "w5-024-the-quest-for-a-spoon", title: "The quest for a spoon", pay: 18360, lib: 5, text: "Pip went to find a lost spoon. He went past a bog and wore mud in his fur. His tail saved him from a deep hole. At last he found a chest. He pried its lid up with one paw. The troop saw all the gold and cried out. Pip shut the lid. He still had soup to eat. The spoon lay under the chest, where it held one short leg still." },
  { id: "w5-165-the-jury-snack-deadlock", title: "The jury snack deadlock", pay: 18360, lib: 5, text: "The troop sat as a jury. They all said yes to the case at once. Then they had to pick a lunch. Gus asked for pie, and May for soup. Pip chose cake, which made both sides cross. Dot sent a note to the judge. It said we are stuck. He sent in ten plain rolls. The troop gave their reply at once and asked never to serve as a jury again." },
  { id: "w5-206-the-lasso-laundry-line", title: "The lasso laundry line", pay: 18360, lib: 5, text: "May joins the rope game. The troop ties hoops for each throw. May fails at each hoop but hooks a pile of wet coats. She lifts them up onto the rope. They dry in the sun while Rex wins the prize. Dot pays May to wash her coats too. Rex asks what he won. His prize is a clean shirt, and May gets the money used to pay for it." },
  { id: "w5-192-the-copier-portrait", title: "The copier portrait", pay: 18630, lib: 5, text: "Gus put his face on the copy box. The troop saw his nose on each memo. Rex asked who had made the new logo. Dot said the box had. Rex asked for more. Gus tried to clean the glass, but Rex said stop. He liked his new logo. Gus now had to put his face on the glass each week. He lost all taste for the prank by June." },
  { id: "w5-238-the-love-nest-zoning", title: "The love nest zoning", pay: 18630, lib: 5, text: "Ivy and Ned build a nest in a tree. The troop calls it a love nest. Dot reads the town rules and says it needs a pass. Ned says birds need none. Dot asks him to prove he is a bird. Ned sings, but Ivy says he can not fly. They move the nest to the floor and call it a rug. Dot says yes to the rug, which keeps the mud off their feet." },
  { id: "w5-205-the-train-tea-whistle", title: "The train tea whistle", pay: 18630, lib: 5, text: "Ned owns a train that makes no noise. The troop fails to see it at the stop. Dot lends him a bell. He rings it and gets every cow in town to trail it. The train moves at a crawl with cows on its rails. Ned asks for a pipe to use. Dot gives him a tea pot. The train now stops for tea at every stop, and the cows stay home for milk." },
  { id: "w5-226-the-love-letter-rent", title: "The love letter rent", pay: 18630, lib: 5, text: "Pip sends a love note to May. He says her smile is worth all the gold in town. The troop reads it in error and feels he has found a mine. They dig under the porch of May. Dot asks what they seek. Pip shows her the note. May comes out with a bill for the porch. Pip sees the price of a smile when it comes with six bills to fix a porch." },
  { id: "w5-222-the-villain-chair-warranty", title: "The villain chair warranty", pay: 18630, lib: 5, text: "Rex spins in his tall chair to greet the troop. The chair spins on and on. Dot tries the brake, but it snaps off. Rex yells that he will rule the world once each turn. Pip puts a broom in the wheel and stops him. Rex asks who broke his chair. Dot hands him the sales slip. His next plot is to get his coins back from the chair shop." },
  { id: "w5-233-the-rival-love-duet", title: "The rival love duet", pay: 18630, lib: 5, text: "Bo and Rex both sing for May. The troop roars at each tune. May asks them to sing as one so she can judge. Each voice jars, and the panes shake. Dot shuts the glass and turns the duet into a quiet show. May likes the moves and hires both to mime at her shop. Bo and Rex vie to stay quiet. Their next duet has no words at all." },
  { id: "w5-171-the-rubber-jewel", title: "The rubber jewel", pay: 18630, lib: 5, text: "May stole a ruby from a hall. Her troop met her by the van. Dot let it fall. It went to the far side of the road. It was a soft prop. May went back to ask why. The owner said the real gem had been gone for weeks. May said she would help find it if she could keep the ball. They hired her to guard the empty case all day." },
  { id: "w5-244-the-romance-novel-route", title: "The romance novel route", pay: 18630, lib: 5, text: "Dot reads that love must start in a storm. She goes out with the troop when rain falls. Bo stays at home and makes tea. Dot comes back wet and cross. Bo gives her a towel. She reads the next page, where the hero gives a towel. Dot shuts the book. Bo asks for it to level his chair. Their first date is tea by a chair held level by a soggy love tale." },
  { id: "w5-241-the-matching-scarf", title: "The matching scarf", pay: 18630, lib: 5, text: "Pip gives May a scarf to match his own. The troop feels it looks sweet. Dot finds that both wraps are parts of one long strip. Pip and May can not walk apart. They try a date, but each takes a fork to a cake at the far end. Dot cuts the scarf in two. May eats plum, Pip eats pear, and both agree that two short wraps make lunch much less messy." },
  { id: "w5-209-the-tumbleweed-post-office", title: "The tumbleweed post office", pay: 18900, lib: 5, text: "Dot ties a note to a dry weed. Wind rolls it to town. The troop goes with it to see if it gets to the post hut. It rolls past the door and into the yard of Rex. Rex reads the note. It asks him to keep weeds out of the lane. Dot holds out her paw for a mail fee. Rex pays with a new weed and asks her to send his reply." },
  { id: "w5-166-the-verdict-stamp", title: "The verdict stamp", pay: 18900, lib: 5, text: "Rex made a stamp that said wrong to save the court time. Dot used it on the first file. It was a claim for a leaky roof. The troop heard the judge blame the roof. Rex said the stamp was fine and the file was wrong. Dot took him out in the rain. He found all the proof he could want on his wet fur. He told the crew to fix the roof." },
  { id: "w5-237-the-mistaken-love-charm", title: "The mistaken love charm", pay: 18900, lib: 5, text: "Bo buys a charm to make Dot love him. He wears it to the troop feast. Dot asks him to pass the salt. Bo feels the charm has won. She asks Gus the same thing. Gus gets no nod. Dot sees the charm and reads its tag. It says charm for soup. Bo puts it in his bowl. The soup is fine, and he asks for one more date with it." },
  { id: "w5-197-the-bank-robber-bond", title: "The bank robber bond", pay: 18900, lib: 5, text: "Bo went to the bank to ask for gold. The clerk asked if he would like a loan. Bo said no, but the troop liked that plan more. Dot read the terms and said the loan cost too much. Bo put his sack on the desk and left. The clerk put forms in it. Bo got a bill for the time spent on his loan. He paid it with his own gold." },
  { id: "w5-217-the-secret-agent-beard", title: "The secret agent beard", pay: 18900, lib: 5, text: "Bo wears a false beard to spy on Rex. The troop says he is too easy to spot. Dot gives him a plain coat to use. Bo goes to the cafe and sits near Rex. Rex asks why he is there. Bo says for tea. Rex gives him a job since that is the first clear reply he has heard all day. Bo tells the troop that the enemy now pays his wages." },
  { id: "w5-242-the-love-quiz-referee", title: "The love quiz referee", pay: 18900, lib: 5, text: "Bo and Ivy take a quiz to see if they match. The troop reads each query aloud. Bo likes rain. Ivy likes sun. Bo likes pie. Ivy likes soup. Dot asks what both like. They say sleep. Dot ends the quiz and gives them two soft pads. They nap while the troop has a row about the score. When they wake, they agree not to take a quiz till they have eaten lunch." },
  { id: "w5-232-the-raincoat-rescue", title: "The raincoat rescue", pay: 18900, lib: 5, text: "Gus sees Dot stand in the rain and gives her his coat. She gives a nod and runs home. The troop roars for his kind heart. Gus stays in the rain with his tail round his bag. Dot comes back with a spare coat. It is tiny. Gus wears it on his head. Dot says that is where all his best ideas seem to leak out, and they use a large shade hat." },
  { id: "w5-234-the-secret-admirer-stamp", title: "The secret admirer stamp", pay: 18900, lib: 5, text: "Ivy gets a box from a shy fan. It holds a plum and no name. The troop tries to guess who sent it. Dot looks at the stamp. It has a paw print made by Ned. Ivy gives Ned a hug for the plum. He says he sent a whole crate. Dot takes a trail of pits to Gus. Ivy says Gus saved her from a belly ache, then asks for the crate to store her notes in." },
  { id: "w5-188-the-decoy-moustache", title: "The decoy beard", pay: 18900, lib: 5, text: "Bo wore a false beard to enter the vault. His troop wore wigs. Dot used glue to hold each beard in place. At the door a fan blew the wigs off. The guard let them in as a choir on tour. Bo sang while Dot took coins. They could not flee till the guard heard the whole song. Bo had to hum the last verse since the words were in his lost wig." },
  { id: "w5-243-the-ice-cream-reunion", title: "The ice cream reunion", pay: 18900, lib: 5, text: "May meets Ned after years apart. The troop hopes for a grand talk. Ned gives her an ice cream. May takes it and asks what he has done all these years. Ned says he has sold ice cream. Dot asks why he never wrote. Ned holds up his messy paws. May buys him a spoon and a pen. He puts his first note on the paper wrap while she eats his whole stock." },
  { id: "w5-198-the-apology-form", title: "The apology form", pay: 19170, lib: 5, text: "Rex lost the troop pay. He said sorry and gave Dot a form. She had to sign to say he was sorry. Dot asked where the pay was. Rex gave her a new form to ask for a form. Dot made him sign the first form. She wrote that he owed them his own pay. He gave that pay to the troop. Rex had to fill out six forms to ask for it back." },
  { id: "w5-160-the-clock-overtime", title: "The clock overtime", pay: 19170, lib: 5, text: "Gus put his name in at dawn and left at dusk. Rex paid him for one hour. The clock had died. The troop knew Gus had done the work, but Rex asked for a time stamp. Dot put the dead clock on the desk of Rex. She asked him to fix it in the paid hour. He spent all night at it and gave Gus his wages prior to his next try." },
  { id: "w5-249-the-red-hat-date", title: "The red hat date", pay: 19170, lib: 5, text: "Ivy waits for Rex in a red hat. The troop wears red hats too, so Rex goes to the wrong table. Gus eats the cake Rex gave him. Dot asks Rex to read the names on the place cards. Rex finds Ivy and gives her a bloom. Ivy says she likes cake more. Gus takes back the empty dish and asks for the bloom in trade. Ivy sends both to the cake shop." },
  { id: "w5-078-the-hatbox-witness", title: "The hatbox witness", pay: 19170, lib: 5, text: "May says she saw the thief from a hat box. Dot asks how she got in. May says she slept there. The troop looks at the tiny box. May can fit one paw in it. Dot asks her to show the view. May puts her eye to the hole. She sees a face on a sign. The thief is a model for cheap hats. The lost coins roll out when May lifts the hat box." },
  { id: "w5-228-the-fake-wedding-cake", title: "The fake wedding cake", pay: 19170, lib: 5, text: "May and Gus act as bride and groom so they can get cake. The troop gives gifts too. Dot asks where the vows are. Gus says he is still at work on them. May asks for a slice while they wait. Dot gives them a cake made of wood. It suits the false vows. May and Gus buy real cake, share it with the troop, and keep the wood one as their table." },
  { id: "w5-053-the-dry-paw-clue", title: "The dry paw clue", pay: 19170, lib: 5, text: "Rain falls all day. A pie is gone from the hut. Dot looks at each paw in the troop. Only May has dry fur. Dot feels sure she has her thief. May shows her a hole in the roof. Her bed is wet too. She dried her paws at the fire, where the chef ate the pie right out of the pan. Dot puts the empty pan in jail and gives May a towel." },
  { id: "w5-247-the-two-picnic-blankets", title: "The two picnic blankets", pay: 19170, lib: 5, text: "Bo and Dot each plan a meal. The troop helps carry their bags. They reach the hill and lay two mats side by side. Bo has bread but no jam. Dot has jam but no bread. They join the meals and sit close. Rex says the match is fine. Then rain falls. Both lack a cover. The troop uses one tree while Bo and Dot each get a mat to wrap round their head." },
  { id: "w5-174-the-merger-of-snack-clubs", title: "The merger of snack clubs", pay: 19170, lib: 5, text: "Gus ran a pie club. May ran a soup club. Rex made them one club to save money. The troop now got one bowl with pie in soup. Dot said she liked one at a time. Rex said she had fear of new ideas. She sold the bowls as dog food and used the coins to buy two lunch tins. Rex gave the firm his best sales chart yet. It had a dog on it." },
  { id: "w5-219-the-rooftop-chase-lift", title: "The rooftop chase lift", pay: 19170, lib: 5, text: "Gus runs after Bo over the roofs. The troop roars as he leaps a gap. Dot takes the lift and waits at the next roof. She grabs Bo by his tail when he lands. Gus asks why she did not make the leap. Dot says the lift was free. Gus pays for his torn shoes, and Dot rides down with Bo, who asks if the lift can be used to flee too." },
  { id: "w5-250-the-vow-in-the-wind", title: "The vow in the wind", pay: 19170, lib: 5, text: "May and Bo write vows on loose cards. Wind takes the cards with no time to read them. Dot runs for the pages. She gets a store list and a rent bill in their place. May reads that she will buy milk. Bo vows to pay rent. The troop roars since those vows are of some use. Dot finds the real vows later and uses them to wrap the cake they take home." },
  { id: "w5-148-the-rocket-pet-door", title: "The rocket pet door", pay: 19440, lib: 5, text: "May took her pet frog onto the ship. It leapt at the red door knob. The troop ran to stop it. Dot hid the knob with a cup. The frog sat on the cup for the whole trip. When they got home, it would not move. May gave it a fly. Dot cut a small pet door in the main door. The frog leapt out for the fly, and May freed the knob at last." },
  { id: "w5-211-the-saloon-milk-duel", title: "The saloon milk duel", pay: 19440, lib: 5, text: "Gus asks for a very stiff drink in town. The troop goes still. Dot gives him warm milk with five heaps of sugar. Gus tips some on his hat and chair, then asks for more. Soon he is stuck to the seat. Rex gives him a drink to free him. It is plain water. Gus says the town is soft, but his hat stays on the floor since the sugar has glued it there." },
  { id: "w5-214-the-sunset-ride-invoice", title: "The sunset ride invoice", pay: 19440, lib: 5, text: "Rex rides west as the red sun sinks. He has saved the town. The troop waves him off. After five ticks he rides back. His horse is owned by Dot, and she wants it home prior to dark. Rex tries to state why he must leave. Dot gives him a broom. He can ride that all night if he wants. Rex walks home, and the broom has a fine view of the red sun." },
  { id: "w5-057-the-blue-ink-trail", title: "The blue ink trail", pay: 19710, lib: 5, text: "May finds blue marks on her clean floor. She calls Dot to solve the case. Dot looks for blue paws in the troop. No one has them. But Pip has a blue tail. He used it as a brush to make a map. Dot reads the trail as lines on a map. It leads to the milk jar, which Pip has put on the roof. Dot gets it and hands Pip a mop to draw his next map." },
  { id: "w5-069-the-case-of-the-double-hat", title: "The case of the double hat", pay: 19710, lib: 5, text: "Dot sees a thief in a tall red hat. She stops Rex, who wears the same hat. He waves at May, who wears one too. The troop has a whole box of them. Dot goes back to the scene and finds red paint on a leaf. Rex has red paint on his tail. He wore the hat on it to fool her. Dot asks him to raise both paws and his tail. The lost cake drops out." },
  { id: "w5-239-the-candlelit-invoice", title: "The candlelit invoice", pay: 19710, lib: 5, text: "Rex takes May to a dim cafe. The troop waits out front to hear how it goes. Rex asks for the best meal for all. He can not see the bill in the dark. May sets a wick on fire and reads it aloud. Rex goes pale. Dot gets a big lamp from the road. The bill is for a whole troop. Rex has asked for a meal for all, and they come in to help him eat." },
  { id: "w5-227-the-balcony-vine", title: "The balcony vine", pay: 19710, lib: 5, text: "Bo sings under the high porch of Dot. His song goes on so long that the troop can not sleep. Dot lets down a vine to pull him up. Bo feels it means she loves him. She hands him a cup of tea and shuts the door. Dot asks him to sip it while it is hot. His lips stay busy. The troop rests while Bo looks at the cup and waits for more tea." },
  { id: "w5-236-the-train-station-farewell", title: "The train station farewell", pay: 19980, lib: 5, text: "Pip runs to stop the train May is on. The troop waves from the track. Pip yells that she must stay. May leans out and asks why. He holds up her lunch. She left it on the table. May takes the bag with her tail and gives him a kiss. The train goes. Pip finds her pass in his paw. It had stuck to the bag. He has to run after the train once more." },
  { id: "w5-204-the-cactus-shade-claim", title: "The cactus shade claim", pay: 19980, lib: 5, text: "Bo buys a patch of land with one plant. He says the troop can rent its shade. At noon the shade is tiny. Dot lies flat and fits under it. Rex tries and gets a thorn in his tail. Bo asks for a fee to pull it out. Dot says she can pay him with shade from her hat. By dusk Bo gives the land in trade for the hat. The troop gets the plant as well." },
  { id: "w5-276-the-art-school-apple", title: "The art school apple", pay: 20790, lib: 5, text: "Sol gave an art class with an apple on a desk. Tess drew it as a box, sure that bold ideas would win stars. Sol asked her to bite the apple. Her furry paws held the round fruit, and her teeth left a round mark. Tess drew that shape next. The class could see what she had seen. They ate the fruit after the class. Sol put the box on the wall too, with a label that said Box, not Apple." },
  { id: "w5-055-the-echo-witness", title: "The echo witness", pay: 21060, lib: 5, text: "Pip hears a voice shout thief in the cave. He leads the troop in with a torch. No one is there. He calls out who said that. The cave asks him the same thing. Pip goes red under his fur. Dot taps his paw and tells him to ask a fresh query. He asks where the pie is. Gus gives a laugh in the dark. The sound leads them to Gus and his pie. Dot lets the cave ask him for a slice." },
  { id: "w5-253-the-nature-film-tame-roar", title: "The nature film tame roar", pay: 21060, lib: 5, text: "Cam shot a film about the wild woods. He asked Dot for a great roar. Dot gave a soft peep. Cam put a roar on tape, but it went on while Dot sat still and took fleas from her fur. Dot asked for the real sound. Cam shot her paws as she took seeds from a shell. The film used that quiet scene. Fans tried her neat trick at home. Cam put the roar tape away and paid Dot a whole bowl of seeds." },
  { id: "w5-289-the-jazz-club-soup-spoon", title: "The jazz club soup spoon", pay: 21060, lib: 5, text: "Ezra sang jazz by the food stand. Gale let a spoon fall in a bowl. The furry band took the clang as a cue and chose a new key. Gale held the spoon up to show the cause. Ezra used the new key for one verse, then came back to the tune. Gale moved the bowls away from the stage. The next clang meant soup was ready. The band took a real break and ate from quiet cups prior to the final set." },
  { id: "w5-257-the-makeover-show-paint-chair", title: "The makeover show paint chair", pay: 21330, lib: 5, text: "Jay ran a show that gave old rooms a new look. Kit asked for a chair with a tail slot. Jay made the old chair gold but left the seat solid. Kit sat on its edge and fell off. Jay tried it and felt the same pinch in his fur. They cut a neat slot and made its edges blunt, then put on fresh paint. Kit sat in it for the last shot. The gold shone, but the slot gave her cause to smile." },
  { id: "w5-193-the-gold-sack-receipt", title: "The gold sack receipt", pay: 21600, lib: 5, text: "Dot took gold from a vault but left a bill. The troop asked why. Dot said the owner must know how much was gone. The owner read it and found she had taken one coin too few. He sent the spare coin by post. Dot said the mail fee cost more than the coin. The owner sent her a rare stamp. Dot now had a stamp worth more than all the gold. She left the gold and took just the stamp books after that." },
  { id: "w5-284-the-poetry-rhyme-fee", title: "The poetry rhyme fee", pay: 21600, lib: 5, text: "Cy ran a verse club and took a coin for each line that did not rhyme. Dora read a poem about rain on her fur. The last word was Roof. Cy asked for a rhyme. Dora put a pail under the leaky club roof. Its drips rang in the pause. The troop kept time with their paws. Cy used the fees to fix the leak and ended the rhyme tax. Dora read the poem again next week in a dry room, with no need for a pail." },
  { id: "w5-262-the-romance-rose-cart", title: "The romance rose cart", pay: 22140, lib: 5, text: "Bram got a cart of roses for Cia in the love film. Cia had no room for them in her small flat. The furry actor left the cart in her door in hope of a kiss. Cia asked him to move it so she could go to work. Bram gave the roses to the park crew and went with her to the bus. The scene ended with a wave, not a kiss. He kept one rose in a cup where her tail would not knock it over." },
  { id: "w5-251-the-soap-actor-and-the-twin-door", title: "The soap actor and the twin door", pay: 22140, lib: 5, text: "Alf was a lost twin in a soap show. Bea stood by the door, set to gasp when he came in. Alf came too soon. Bea gave her gasp to an empty chair, for his tail was stuck on a coat peg. The crew had to stop. Bea freed him, then wrote Enter on the right page. They did the scene once more. Alf came in on cue. Bea gave a real gasp this time, since he wore her coat and all her hats at once." },
  { id: "w5-280-the-gallery-snack-label", title: "The gallery snack label", pay: 22140, lib: 5, text: "Zed set fruit on a stand at the art show. Ada asked if it was art or a snack. The furry host said it could be both. Ada took a grape, and Zed cried that the work was not whole now. She put it back, but the bite mark was there. Zed wrote a new label about bites. Ada paid for the grape and asked for a clear food table. Zed made one by the door. The next guest could eat there and leave the art alone." },
  { id: "w5-281-the-novel-chapter-cake", title: "The novel chapter cake", pay: 22140, lib: 5, text: "Ames wrote a tale about a baker who lost her cake. Bess read each part and asked where it was. Ames added a new quest each time, his pen firm in a furry paw. At last Bess drew a cake on the final page and wrote Found It. Ames saw how tired she was. He wrote a real close at the bake shop door. The cake was there on a cart. Bess paid for the book and made a cake to eat while he wrote his name on the cover." },
  { id: "w5-286-the-poster-tiny-date", title: "The poster tiny date", pay: 22140, lib: 5, text: "Ed made a vivid sign for the troop show. Faye could read the huge title from afar but could not find the date. Ed held his paw by tiny print near a blue star. Faye came close, her fur flat on the wall. She asked for a large date and a small star. Ed drew it in bold type and moved the star to the edge. The crowd came on the right day. Ed kept a copy by his desk to test each new date from afar." },
  { id: "w5-255-the-talent-judge-sock", title: "The talent judge sock", pay: 22140, lib: 5, text: "Flo sang a clear tune, but Gus gave her low marks for her plain socks. Flo asked the judge to wear fine socks and sing it too. Gus put a gold pair on his paws, held the mic, and made a rough peep. The crowd loved the joke. Gus said the socks did not help. Flo sang once more and got fair marks. She kept the plain socks for the last round, with her tail round the stool so no stage cloth could trip her." },
  { id: "w5-288-the-choir-late-echo", title: "The choir late echo", pay: 22140, lib: 5, text: "Ewan led the choir in a stone hall. Flo sang the last note, then heard it come back after the next verse began. The echo made the furry troop lose their place. Ewan tried a quick beat, which made more noise. Flo hung thick rugs on the back wall. They sang once more, and the words came in order. Ewan kept the rugs for each show. Flo took one home after the final song. It was her own rug, and her floor felt cold." },
  { id: "w5-295-the-cartoon-cliff-rail", title: "The cartoon cliff rail", pay: 22410, lib: 5, text: "Ivan drew a hero who ran off a cliff and hung in the air. Lena asked why his tail could not grab a tree. Ivan said the fall had a joke in it, his furry face grave. Lena drew a tree in the next panel and let the tail catch it. Ivan added an odd face as the hero swung back to the path. The strip still had a joke. The hero could do his task now. Lena drew a rail in the last panel for the next safe trip." },
  { id: "w5-278-the-mime-glass-test", title: "The mime glass test", pay: 22410, lib: 5, text: "Val mimed a glass wall at the fair. Willa tried to hand the furry actor a coin, but Val would not leave his pose. She put the coin on the floor and went away. Val bent down to get it. The crowd saw him pass the wall he had made. He gave a shy bow. On the next round he mimed a door in the wall and used it to take each coin. Willa came back with tea and used that door to give it to him." },
  { id: "w5-290-the-piano-lid-pledge", title: "The piano lid pledge", pay: 22410, lib: 5, text: "Finn kept the piano lid shut so his grand coat could lie on it. Hope asked the furry star how the sound would reach the hall. Finn hit a chord, and it came out dull. Hope hung the coat on a hook and put the lid up. The next chord rang clear. Finn did the whole show in his plain vest. The crowd did not miss the coat. Hope put its hook by the door, far from the keys and lid, for each later night." },
  { id: "w5-294-the-art-fair-price-frame", title: "The art fair price frame", pay: 22410, lib: 5, text: "Ian put a small piece of art in a huge gold frame at the fair. Lana asked what it cost. The furry host named a high price based on the frame. Lana liked the art but had no wall space for all the gold. Ian took it out and gave a price for the paper alone. Lana paid for it and put it in a plain book. Ian used the empty frame round his stall sign. Its shine led the crowd to the real art for sale below." },
  { id: "w5-271-the-rock-band-shoe-beat", title: "The rock band shoe beat", pay: 22410, lib: 5, text: "Max got heavy boots to make his drum beat sound tough. Nora heard him stomp off time at the drum. His tail hit a plate at each wrong step. Nora set a small clock by the drum and asked him to tap in plain socks. Max found the beat again. He kept the boots by the door for the walk home and did the show in socks. Nora gave him a loud cheer. That was the only extra crash for the final tune to end well." },
  { id: "w5-282-the-stage-dragon-fan", title: "The stage dragon fan", pay: 22410, lib: 5, text: "Axel wore a beast head in the troop play. Bree blew smoke into it with a fan. The furry actor could not see his cue. He gave a roar at the wrong king and fell in a prop well. Bree cut the smoke and got him out. They put the fan by the back wall so smoke would flow past his head. Axel saw the next cue and gave his roar on time. Bree left the fan on low after the show to cool the hot suits." },
  { id: "w5-287-the-puppet-crown-swap", title: "The puppet crown swap", pay: 22410, lib: 5, text: "Eli used a new doll for each royal role in the play. Fern had to pull ten furry kings on cords at the back of the small stage. Their tails tied knots in the cords. Eli took a pause and moved them apart. Fern used one doll and a new crown for each king. The troop knew each role by its hat. Eli put the spare dolls by the door, where young fans could pose with them. No cords could tie knots in those tails now." },
  { id: "w5-265-the-science-film-blinking-panel", title: "The science film blinking panel", pay: 22410, lib: 5, text: "Finn sat at a panel full of lamps in the space film. Gia asked him to press the key that would start the ship. None had a label. The furry actor took a guess and a lamp went out by his tail. Gia ended the take and wrote Start on one key and Stop on the next. Finn had a clear task now. The scene went well in one take. Gia left the other lamps off, so fans could see which key sent the ship on its way." },
  { id: "w5-256-the-news-desk-tail-peek", title: "The news desk tail peek", pay: 22410, lib: 5, text: "Hal read the news at a desk too high for his stool. Ivy saw only the top of his fur on the TV. Hal tried to sit on his tail as a pad, but it slid out. Ivy took a firm box and set the stool on it. Hal read the next item with his whole face in view. A guest asked why he was so tall. Hal let them see the box after the show. Ivy put a safe step by it for each guest to use." },
  { id: "w5-258-the-travel-host-toll-lesson", title: "The travel host toll lesson", pay: 22410, lib: 5, text: "Lou said a plain toll booth was a lost altar on his tour show. Mae, who ran the booth, asked the furry host for two coins. Lou tried a magic chant but did not pay. Mae kept the gate shut until he did. The crew shot the whole scene with the real booth name in view. Lou saw his error and got a map. His next show told the troop how to cross the creek, with no chant and no fake tale about the old toll booth." },
  { id: "w5-261-the-stunt-pool-splash", title: "The stunt pool splash", pay: 22410, lib: 5, text: "Ash had to leap into a pool for the chase film. Bina asked how deep it was. Ash posed on the rail but did not check. Bina put in a pole and found only a foot of water. The furry actor came down and let her fill it first. They tried a leap from a low step, then did the full shot. Ash hit the water with a great spray and no sore paws. Bina put the depth on a sign and used the pole to hang their wet coats." },
  { id: "w5-270-the-epic-film-map", title: "The epic film map", pay: 22410, lib: 5, text: "Leo held up a map to show where his army would march. Mina saw the route cross the page edge and jump to the other side. The furry actor had put two maps the wrong way round. Mina gave one a turn and found the road ran by a lake. Leo gave a new talk about the safe shore path. The troop took that route in the next shot. Mina made a neat fold, and the final fight could begin in a place that fans knew from the tale." },
  { id: "w5-283-the-critic-blank-notebook", title: "The critic blank notebook", pay: 22410, lib: 5, text: "Bo wrote a harsh piece about a play while the stage was still dark. Cora saw his notes from her seat. She asked the furry guest what the play was about. Bo did not know. Cora lent him a clean page and asked him to watch the first scene. He found two jokes and wrote them down. His final piece gave those parts high marks and named one slow scene. Cora kept the old page as proof that a neat line could be full of empty air." },
  { id: "w5-291-the-record-label-rush", title: "The record label rush", pay: 22410, lib: 5, text: "Gus asked Iona to sing her new song that night. The furry star had only half the words. Gus said the rest could wait for the next disc. Iona sang one verse and sat down in the long empty pause. Gus heard how odd it was. He gave her a week to end the tale. Iona wrote about the lost kite at home with its owner. The song came out whole. Gus kept a blank disc on his desk to show what a rush could yield." },
  { id: "w5-254-the-sitcom-couch-move", title: "The sitcom couch move", pay: 22680, lib: 5, text: "Dax asked to move the couch on the set so he could walk to the door. Eve said it must stay for the wide shot. Dax tried to hop over it, but his tail hit Eve with a thump. They had to stop the take. Eve moved the couch just a bit. The shot was the same, and Dax had a path. He came in with ease. The joke came from his odd hat now, and Eve could drink her tea with no tail in her cup." },
  { id: "w5-292-the-dance-film-close-shot", title: "The dance film close shot", pay: 22680, lib: 5, text: "Hal shot Joss as she did her dance, but kept the frame tight on her face. The furry star asked him to watch the film. He saw a smile and no steps at all. Joss asked for a wide shot with her tail and both paws in view. Hal moved the lens back and shot the whole dance again. Fans could copy the steps now. He kept one close shot for the final bow. Her feet were still then, and her face could have its turn." },
  { id: "w5-293-the-stage-rain-bucket", title: "The stage rain bucket", pay: 22680, lib: 5, text: "Hank put real water on the stage for the storm scene. Kira slid as she went on it, and her tail held the rail. The furry actor asked for a dry floor. Hank used blue cloth and a sound tape for the next storm. Kira could walk and say her lines with ease. The crowd knew it was rain, but no one got wet. Hank used the water left in his pail to mop the floor after the show. No actor had to cross it then." },
  { id: "w5-252-the-quiz-buzzer-loaf", title: "The quiz buzzer loaf", pay: 22680, lib: 5, text: "Bex knew each quiz fact, but her bell was mute. Cole told her to clap if she knew the next one. Her soft claps could not reach him. Bex hit a spoon on a loaf tin from the snack desk. The clang rang clear. Cole gave each guest a tin so the round was fair. Bex won by one point. She took the cash prize and got warm bread. They ate it from the same tins, and Cole kept one as a spare bell for the next show." },
  { id: "w5-279-the-dance-shoe-glue", title: "The dance shoe glue", pay: 22680, lib: 5, text: "Wes wore old shoes to each dance. He felt they gave him luck. Yara saw a sole peel away as he spun. His tail held a rail so he could sit to mend it. The glue took time to set. Yara lent him a plain spare pair for the show. Wes did each step well and saw that the skill was his, not in the old soles. He put the old shoes on a shelf at home. The new pair fit his paws with no need for glue." },
  { id: "w5-274-the-radio-play-fruit-bite", title: "The radio play fruit bite", pay: 22680, lib: 5, text: "Poe ate an apple while he read a royal tale on radio. Quin heard the crisp bite and felt sure a door had split. The furry actor tried to speak with his mouth full. Quin ended the take and gave him a plate out of the booth. Poe ate the rest, wiped his paws, and came back to read the tale in a clear voice. Quin taped one bite for a later food stall scene. The king could now rule in peace until the play asked him to eat." },
  { id: "w5-260-the-series-recap-chain", title: "The series recap chain", pay: 22950, lib: 5, text: "Paz shot a recap for the new show. Rue asked for a recap of that one, since it went on too long. The furry crew made a third clip to sum up the last two. Soon the day was gone and no new scene was done. Paz drew the last plot on one small card. Rue held it in view for ten beats, then began the new scene. The troop saw the new tale at last. Paz filed the old clips and kept the card for next week." },
  { id: "w5-263-the-horror-prop-squeal", title: "The horror prop squeal", pay: 22950, lib: 5, text: "Clem took the lid off a box in the scary film. Dara put on a loud wail. The box held a plain comb. Clem leapt so hard his tail hit the lid. The crew had to fix it. Dara used a quiet creak on the next take. Clem saw the comb, gave his fur a brush, and found a key in its case. The scene had a real clue now. Dara saved the loud wail for the last door, where the key did not fit and the hero had cause to fear." },
  { id: "w5-298-the-quiz-prize-bill", title: "The quiz prize bill", pay: 22950, lib: 5, text: "Jules won a huge piano on the quiz show. Nola asked the furry guest to sign for it. Jules saw that cart hire to get it home cost more than his rent. He asked for a small drum. Nola read the prize list and let him pick one that fit in his bag. Jules hit it on the bus home, then quit when asked. Nola added cart costs to the prize cards. The next guest knew the full price prior to using a pen to claim a shiny prize." },
  { id: "w5-277-the-grand-mural-tiny-brush", title: "The grand mural tiny brush", pay: 22950, lib: 5, text: "Tom took a tiny brush to paint a mural on the town hall. Una saw him make one dot per hour while his tail held the paint can. She gave him a wide brush for the broad blue sky. Tom used it, then saved the tiny one for bird eyes. The mural was done by dusk. Una asked him to sign it, and he chose the tiny brush for that final mark. The troop could now see both the whole sky and the small birds from the lane." },
  { id: "w5-285-the-museum-arrow-loop", title: "The museum arrow loop", pay: 22950, lib: 5, text: "Don put signs on the art hall floor to lead the troop round the rooms. Etta read them and came back to the same bowl six times. Her tail drew a dusty ring by it. Don saw one sign aimed the wrong way. He gave it a turn and took the whole route with Etta. They found the exit at last. Don swept the ring away and gave Etta free entry next month. He added a small map she could hold in her paw on the next tour." },
  { id: "w5-259-the-game-show-prize-goat", title: "The game show prize goat", pay: 22950, lib: 5, text: "Ned won a goat suit on the game show. Ora asked him to pose in it. The suit had four leg holes but no tail hole. Ned could move only in short hops. Ora bent down to cut a slot as the crew stood by. Ned could walk with ease, then gave a loud stage bleat that made Ora leap from her chair. They kept that take as the last gag. Ned took the suit home for the troop play next year, with his tail free to sway." },
  { id: "w5-296-the-soap-show-clock", title: "The soap show clock", pay: 23220, lib: 5, text: "Jake shot a soap scene in which Mara had to wait for her tea. Five shows went by and the cup still had not come. The furry actor asked if her guest must have a dry mouth for a month. Jake put tea in the next scene and let her drink. Mara could talk about the lost ring at last. Jake kept a clock on the set after that. Each long pause had to leave room for the plot to move. The tea pot had a real place by the stove." },
  { id: "w5-268-the-western-film-dust-bag", title: "The western film dust bag", pay: 23220, lib: 5, text: "Jem rode a prop cart in the old west film. Kara shook dust from a bag to make the scene look wild. The furry actor got dust in his nose and could not say his line. Kara swept the track and let the cart make a small cloud on its own. Jem spoke with a clear voice at last. They gave his hat a rinse after the shot. Kara kept the dust bag for the empty road scene. No one would have to take air from the cloud she made there." },
  { id: "w5-297-the-news-show-fake-crowd", title: "The news show fake crowd", pay: 23490, lib: 5, text: "Jude put a tape of a large crowd at the back of the news set. The furry host said the town plaza was full. Neve saw a wool coat in the tape, but the live day was hot. She asked Jude to show the real view. Two fans and a cart stood in the plaza. Neve told that true count on air. Jude wrote the date on the old tape and kept it for past clips. The next live count came from the plaza lens with no old coats in view." },
  { id: "w5-264-the-fantasy-sword-size", title: "The fantasy sword size", pay: 23490, lib: 5, text: "Dell got a huge sword for the quest film. Edie asked him to draw it, but his paws could not reach the whole way. Dell gave its case a tilt and the sword hit the stage floor. Edie gave him a short blade made of wood. The furry hero could walk and bow with no help. The shot was bold when she took it from low down. Dell hung the huge sword over the prop shelf. Its only job now was to look grand at the back of the shot." },
  { id: "w5-299-the-costume-coat-hem", title: "The costume coat hem", pay: 23490, lib: 5, text: "Karl wore a long royal coat on stage. Oona had to walk after him with its tail end in her paws. It would catch on seats if she let go. The furry actor saw her lose all her own cues. They put the coat hem up with pins until it came to his knees. Karl could walk alone, and Oona could play her role. The coat was still grand from afar. After the bow Karl took the pins out, and Oona hung it flat for the next show." },
  { id: "w5-272-the-choir-fur-tickle", title: "The choir fur tickle", pay: 23490, lib: 5, text: "Nim wore a plume ruff for the choir show. It made his fur itch, and he gave a cough in the first verse. Opal asked him to take it off, but Nim felt he would look plain. She gave him a blue scarf that lay flat. Nim sang the next verse with a firm voice. The troop heard the tune at last. Opal hung the plume ruff on a music stand as trim. It could look grand there and stay far from each neck, so the whole choir could sing in peace." },
  { id: "w5-300-the-encore-note-card", title: "The encore note card", pay: 23490, lib: 5, text: "Kent sang a last song each time he heard claps. Pru tried to leave the hall, but the furry star began again when she gave a clap on her way out. She held a card that said Good Night. Kent bowed and let the song end. The troop could go home at last. Pru put the card by the mic for the next show. Kent used it after one extra tune, then gave a small wave. The crowd could clap at the close and still walk out of the open door." },
  { id: "w5-273-the-pop-tour-case", title: "The pop tour case", pay: 23760, lib: 5, text: "Odo put ten shiny balls in cases for his pop tour. Pia asked where the drums and mics would fit. The furry star waved at a tiny gap by the van door. Pia took one case lid off. It could hold all the stage gear if the balls came out. Odo kept one ball and left the rest at home. The show began on time with clear sound. Pia put the spare empty cases under the stage, where they held coats and left the aisle free for the crowd." },
  { id: "w5-269-the-musical-bus-fare", title: "The musical bus fare", pay: 23760, lib: 5, text: "Kip sang for five whole tunes while he tried to board a bus in the stage show. Lila stood with her paw on the fare box. The furry star did a dance on the step but did not pay. Lila asked for the coin first. Kip paid, sat down, and sang the rest from his seat. The scene could move at last, with the bus on its way to town. Lila got a short solo at the next stop about the rule that all tails must stay clear of the doors." },
  { id: "w5-266-the-spy-film-cuff", title: "The spy film cuff", pay: 24030, lib: 5, text: "Glen wore gold cuffs in the spy film. One cuff held his tail in a snag as he tried to get the coded note. Hana had to wait as he spun in his chair. They took a break to put plain cloth cuffs on his coat. Glen read the note, then left the room with no snags. Hana kept the gold pair in a prop box for a close shot only. Glen asked for the cloth ones in each chase. A free tail gave him more speed than a bit of gold on his paws." },
  { id: "w5-267-the-film-villain-chair", title: "The film villain chair", pay: 24300, lib: 5, text: "Hugh was a cruel lord in a tall black chair. Iris asked him to turn to face the hero. The chair legs made a noise and held his tail tight. Hugh moved only an inch, then gave a yelp. Iris freed his tail, then put the chair on a board that could roll. Hugh could glide round for the next take. His grim face was good, but the board gave a creak. Iris oiled its axles. Hugh gave his final line at last, with no extra sound to make him seem like a cart full of mice." },
  { id: "w5-275-the-folk-singer-rhyme", title: "The folk singer rhyme", pay: 24570, lib: 5, text: "Rai sang that the mill fell down just to rhyme with town. Rosa ran the mill and asked the furry bard to come see it. The walls stood firm, and the wheel spun in the creek. Rai wrote a new verse about grain and flour. He kept the rhyme with carts that came into town. Rosa gave a cheer at the next show and had bread for the troop. Rai tried more ways to rhyme prior to his song about the road, which also still lay firm and would not crack for a verse." }
);
